What?"\rI was possessed."\rYour soul is mine!"What's going on?"\rI was under possession.",Entered the purifed and protected zone."&\Pn's Pokémon were fully healed."\r...Give."How? What?"E\rI fell to evil spirits despite my training in the mountains..."B\rCome, child! I have purified this space. You can rest here.Iu;␀f[["\rHahaha."Ha?" \rI feel anemic and weak..."\rReady?"	Huh?"\rWhat's going on here?"\rMy hair is gone.."Say what?"<\rMy hair didn't fall out!\nIt was a malevolent spirit!["\rHahaha."Ha?" \rI feel anemic and weak..."\rReady?"	Huh?"\rWhat's going on here?"\rMy hair is gone.."Say what?"<\rMy hair didn't fall out!\nIt was a malevolent spirit!;["\rHahaha."Ha?" \rI feel anemic and weak..."\rReady?"	Huh?"\rWhat's going on here?"\rMy hair is gone.."Say what?"<\rMy hair didn't fall out!\nIt was a malevolent spirit!Iu;␀B[["R\rYou are quite brave for a child. But this will have you running in no time."*\rI'm no longer possessed. Thank you!"8\rOh, you came here so you could challenge Sabrina?" \rThis might help you then."4\rTM121 contains Shadow Punch. It never misses."'\rI wish you luck in your travels.["R\rYou are quite brave for a child. But this will have you running in no time."*\rI'm no longer possessed. Thank you!"8\rOh, you came here so you could challenge Sabrina?" \rThis might help you then."4\rTM121 contains Shadow Punch. It never misses."'\rI wish you luck in your travels.;["R\rYou are quite brave for a child. But this will have you running in no time."*\rI'm no longer possessed. Thank you!"8\rOh, you came here so you could challenge Sabrina?" \rThis might help you then."4\rTM121 contains Shadow Punch. It never misses."'\rI wish you luck in your travels.Iu;␀a[["g\rMisty: You're heading to Celadon City too? It's a beautiful city, full of shops and opportunity."h\rOh, you're going for the gym. I should have guessed as much. Fine, we can have a practice battle."&\rMisty: Good luck with your gym."\bPrimeape".Would you like to take Primeape with you?"Yes"No["h \rMisty: You're heading to Celadon City too? It's a beautiful city, full of shops and opportunity."h\rOh, you're going for the gym. I should have guessed as much. Fine, we can have a practice battle."&\rMisty: Good luck with your gym."\bPrimeape".Would you like to take Primeape with you?"Yes"No;["g\rMisty: You're heading to Celadon City too? It's a beautiful city, full of shops and opportunity."h\rOh, you're going for the gym. I should have guessed as much. Fine, we can have a practice battle."&\rMisty: Good luck with your gym."\bPrimeape".Would you like to take Primeape with you?"Yes"NoIu;␀-[[�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!".\rWould you like to recieve some healing?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"o\rCan't believe you made me fully restore your team, you bastard. This wasn't supposed to even be a thing."`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."9\rYour team should already be at full health, right?"8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto, Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary, Neo Champion,Sygna Buffs]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto, Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary,Neo Champion]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."�\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying! That is, if you don't hit F12 because you're a sore loser or a tryhard."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bThey'll also have some interesting moves too, ranging from moves used by their trainers instead or powerful moves that can only be used under certain conditions."�\bFuthermore, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"�\bBut lastly, and you might find a silver lining in this - I've made it so that not only do you benefit from some damage reduction, the "harder" trainers have a lower chance to show up early."�\bSo if you want to familiarise yourself with the trainers here, it might be good to try this challenge with a lower difficulty first.".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure. Which one would you like me to explain? \ch[1,-1,Crit Rate,Trainer Move,B Move,Passive Skill, Master Passive,Zone,Gradual Healing]"R\bCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages."�\bTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses (rather than their Pokémon). These moves tend to buff the user's Pokémon or their team's side."^\bThey can be used even when the trainer's Pokémon is afflicted with a status condition."}\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. You can identify them by the "descriptor" in the move's name, e.g. Origin Volt Tackle."~\bThey tend to do what the move they're based on does, but with increased power, added effects or the regular effect enhanced."\bThere's usually a condition that has to be met before each B Move can be used, so use that to your advantage to counter them!"�\bIf they don't, they will likely have very little PP instead. Lastly, all trainers only have 1 B Move at most, but there is 1 exception."mPassive Skill - Essentially an extra ability, but they can't be ignored by effects such as Mold Breaker."~\bHow many a Pokémon has is completely arbitrary, though I've tried to limit it to 3 at most, excluding Master Passives."l\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the team's damage dealt and reduces the damage taken."k\bThere are 3 types: Flag Bearer is for all moves and is 10% damage increase and 20% damage reduction."W\bPride is for physical moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."_\bLastly, Spirit is for special moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."`\bZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type by 50%."s\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn. Think of it kinda like Leftovers."T\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika, Red,Red (Thunderbolt),Blue,Leaf]"W\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit."�\bAnyway, his Trainer Move give his Tyranitar's +1 Defense and makes its next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but there are ways to get around it, like Protect."�\bTtar has 2 passives. One gives its moves a higher chance to apply their additional effects and the other prevents its stats from dropping in a sandstorm."s\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move gives her Vaporeon +2 Defense and her side +2 Sp. Defense."�\bLastly, her Vaporeon's passives give it gradual healing when switching in as well as a chance to raise its Evasion after it uses a move."}\bErika's Trainer Move gives her Leafeon's +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, but if the Sun's up, these stat increases are doubled."`\bLeafeon's ability is Chorophyll, so with the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled."t\bThen, its passives don't allow status conditions to be inflicted on it as well as heal it after using a move."@\bIn other words, you really don't want Leafeon in the Sun!"�\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Charizard's +3 Attack, Sp. Attack and Speed and +2 Crit Rate, though its Defense and Sp. Defense are lowered by -1."{\bHis Charizard also has passives which allow its moves to never miss and not require a rechage turn after using them."X\bKnow what that means? It's able to use Blast Burn. Every. Single. Turn. Have fun!"s\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move gives Pikachu +6 Attack and Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since there you only use 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair per battle."h\bIt also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."{\bIts other passives make all its moves critical hits, as well as healing it after it uses a move in Electric Terrain."q\bLast, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a B Move which can only be used when Electric Terrain's active."X\bIf your Pokémon's paralyzed, its Defense and Sp. Defense are also lowered by -1."r\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Defense and +1 Crit Rate, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."~\bAnyway, his Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, one of its passive gives his side +1 Attack and Sp. Attack."�\bAnd then when it attacks, its other passive gives its side +1 Sp. Defense. Lastly, it also doesn't need to recharge after using Hydro Cannon."`\bWith Leaf's Trainer Move, I took a few creative liberties to make it live up to its name."q\bIt provides the Pokémon on her side Gradual Healing, as well as healing them all for 40% of their max HP!"�\bAs for Venusaur's passives, they badly poison your Pokémon and gives them -1 to their defensive stats after they're attacked by it."h\bWith Razor Leaf and a non-recharging Frenzy Plant, it's sure to deal out a ton poison and damage."Y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris, Silver,Giovanni,Giovanni (Ultra)]"q\bMorty's Trainer Move gives +1 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate to his side, as well as setting Tailwind."�\bOne of Ho-oh's passives gives additional stat boosts to its team if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."a\bIts other passive then heals the Pokémon on Ho- oh's side when it uses a move in the Sun."s\bEthan's Trainer Move powers up Lugia's next special move, gives it +1 Accuracy and makes its next move crit."{\bLugia has passives which makes its single target attacks hit all opponents as well as restore PP to Ethan's Trainer Move."k\bLastly, it also has a Spirit Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bLyra's Trainer Move gives +2 Attack and Sp. Attack to a Pokémon on her side and gives them Gradual Healing. But that's not the crazy thing about this sync pair."�\bCelebi has passives which leaves the opponent flinched, trapped and confused after using a move and lowers one of the target's stats by -2."v\bAnnnnd Celebi has Grassy Glide and can set up Grassy Terrain too to give it priority. Talk about a nasty combo!"j\bLastly, it also has a Pride Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."N\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers."O\bAt base, her Trainer Move gives her side +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate."{\bBut if it's Raining, it also powers up the next special attack from her team, making them pack an even bigger punch."�\bOne of Suicune's passives gives its side +4 Sp. Defense if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."�\bIts other passive heals its team after a uses a move under the Rain. I think you get the idea - Rain is dangerous if you're facing Kris!"k\bLastly, it has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."k\bSilver's Trainer Move gives Sneasel +3 Attack and Speed, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."�\bSneasel's B Move, Crushing Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. In theory, that doesn't sound too hard to counter, right?"\bWell, on every hit of a multi-hit move, its passives lower the opposing Pokémon's Speed by -1 while it gets +1 Evasion."~\bIt also gets +1 Crit Rate on each hit of its B Move too, but it doesn't have any other ways of increasing its damage itself."N\bSo at best, you get lucky and OHKO it, while at worst, it's a nuisance."<\bGiovanni's Trainer Move gives his Nidoking +6 Attack."a\bHis Nidoking has a passive to make all its attacks critical hits, including its Max Moves."�\bIts other passive turns Normal moves into Ground moves, allowing it to gain STAB from it. Its Mega Kick is going to hit pretty hard!"�\bThis version of Giovanni has a Trainer Move which gives his side +2 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as making Guzzlord the center of attention."{\bGuzzlord has passives which enable its Stockpile Defense and Sp. Defense boosts to be tripled and shared with its allies."O\bHowever, it can only Stockpile a maximum of 2 times as a result of this."�\bGuzzlord also doesn't have just 1 B Move, but 2! It's the one exception to the "rule" that says there can only be 1 B Move for each sync pair."i\bWhen used, they both remove Stockpiles's stat boosts and restores 1 PP to Giovanni's Trainer Move."�\bThe first one, Guzzling Swallow, can only be used after Stockpile has been used and restores Guzzlord's HP based on how many times it was used."=\bThen, it restores a fixed amount of HP for its allies."�\bThe second one is Gourging Crunch. It can only be used when the Guzzlord's stat boosts for Defense and Sp. Defense are 6 or greater."9\bIt then lowers the target's defensive stats by -1.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Blaziken +4 Attack and +1 Accuracy, sets up Tailwind and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."�\bBlaziken's first passive gives +1 Speed to its side when entering battle, including Mega Evolution, effectively translating to a +2 increase."�\bIts other passive lowers the target's Defense by -2. All in all, very speedy and it can easily snowball if you're not careful."c\bBrendan's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense as well as +1 Crit Rate."u\bHis Latios's first passive powers up its sides' next special moves when entering the battle and Mega Evolving."x\bIts other passive then increases the likelihood of additional effects; if it's a stat drop, it'll be doubled too."p\bIt has Luster Purge, so that'll mean that you'll be taking a lot of special damage if you're not careful!"�\bSteven... is a lot. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4! So let's break him down a bit.\ch[2,-1,Initial State,Shared Traits, Normal Forme,Attack Forme,Defense Forme,Speed Forme]"\bInitially, Deoxys starts in its Normal Forme with 4 Trainer Moves and a passive which gives it +1 Accuracy when switching in."�\bThe first one, "Try This!", sets Psychic Terrain and gives Deoxys +2 Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed and keep Deoxys in its Normal Forme."u\bHis second one, "Attack!", gives Deoxys +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme."�\bThe third one, "Defend!" gives its +4 side Attack and Sp. Attack. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn."r\bLast but not least,"Faster!", gives Deoxys +6 Speed and +3 Evasion and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme."�\bOutside of its inital state, all forms of Deoxys that Steven has have a passive with converts stat drops into stat increases, but not vice versa like Contrary does!"a\bThey all also have Psycho Boost and Zen Headbutt, so I won't be mentioning them elsewhere."`\bIn its Normal Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."{\bIt also has a passive which increase the chance of additional effects, so if it uses Zen Headbutt, be prepared to flinch!"`\bIn its Attack Forme, Deoxys has Protect and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which increases the power of its next physical and special moves, so it might quickly snowball out of control!"a\bIn its Defense Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Iron Defense in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which gives its side +2 Sp. Defense each time a status move is used, so with Iron Defense it'll become very bulky very quickly."^\bIn its Speed Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Double Team in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which sets up Tailwind for its side when a status move is successful the first time it's used in battle."_\bWally's Trainer Move gives his Gardevoir +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Sp. Defense and Crit Rate."�\bGardevoir has 2 passives - the first gives its side +1 Speed when entering battle and Mega Evolving; the other leaves the target confused after a move."�\bGardevoir also has a B Move, Ultimate Dazzling Gleam. It lowers the targets' Attack and Sp. Attack by -4, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks."�\bIt can only be used once, but you can't Protect against it and -4 on your attacking stats will likely force you to switch out your Pokémon."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."�\bApart from that, Kommo-o has passives which allow it to ignore damage reduction from Reflect, Light Screen and Aurora Veil as well as increase the chance for additional effects."�\bThis version of Cynthia's Trainer Move gives Giratina +4 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate. She can also set a Ghost Zone."T\bHer Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Sp. Defense of the target by -1."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move gives her side +4 Defense and Sp. Defense, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll give +6 instead."r\bAs for that, her Lucario has a passive which sets Fighting Zone on entry, so most of the time, it'll be +6."s\bLucario's other passive also depends on Fighting Zone - it heals its side after using a move if it's active."y\bIt also has Superior Aura Sphere, a B Move that never misses and can only be used after Lucario is attacked twice."]\bAfter it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of its side."p\bLastly, Lucario has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."\bCyrus's Trainer Move gives his Darkrai +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy and Crit Rate. In addition, he can set a Dark Zone."�\bDarkrai has passives which power up its moves if the target is asleep, or if it's using a status move, it'll lower a random stat of all opponents by -1."[\bIt does have Dark Void, but even if it misses, its 2nd passive will activate anyway."�\bDawn's Trainer Move gives her side +2 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP."^\bYou might be thinking, why do that, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"i\bCresselia's very tanky, but one of its passives makes it even more so when it has 50% HP or lower."�\bIts other passive also increases the power of its side's special moves if Cresselia uses a status move when it's HP is 50% or lower."P\bIt also has Moonlight for healing, so don't count your chickens too soon!"R\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N, Roxie,Ingo,Emmet]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move gives +2 Accuracy and Crit Rate to a Pokémon on her side, as well as giving +2 Sp. Attack to all Pokémon on her side."�\bRotom has a passive which gives it +1 Evasion when it's hit, as well as another which prevents its Evasion from being lowered."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it gives +6 Attack and Evasion and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition, it has passives which increase the chance of the additional effects its moves and increase their power when Sharpedo is in a pinch."s\bHilbert's Trainer Move gives his Genesect +3 Sp. Attack, +2 Crit Rate and powers up its next special attack."�\bWhen using Techno Blast, Genesect changes form depending on the type the target is weakest to. Its default is also Bug instead of Normal."]\bThen, it makes them weaker to that type and applies an effect corresponding that type."m\bElectric - Paralyze target.\n Fire - Lower target's Attack by -1.\n Ice - 50% chance to freeze target."H\bWater - Lower target's Defense by -1. Bug - No additional effect."d\bLastly, if Genesect lands a super effective hit, its passive lowers the target's Speed by -2."�\bHilda's Trainer Move raises her Victini's Sp. Attack by how much its Attack has been raised, then gives it +3 Crit Rate and gives its team +1 Accuracy."�\bThis is complemented by Victini's passives, which gives it +2 Attack on switching in and turns stat drops into stat increases."y\bThere's even more synergy - Victini has V-Create, so it just keeps getting bulkier and faster each time it's used!"D\bN's Trainer Move gives his Kyurem +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bWhen Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it has a passive which halves the damage it takes while charging and unlocks its B Move, Resonating Noble Roar."|\bIt lowers the Attack, Sp. Attack, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by -2, while it powering up its next physical attack."�\bFreeze Shock then needs to be used again before it can be used again, preventing it from being spammed endlessly (it also has 3 PP)."�\bKyurem also has a passive which allows it to ignore the opponent's enduring effects, but I imagine that won't come up too often."q\bRoxie's Trainer Move gives her Toxtricity +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate and applies Tailwind to her side."W\bToxtricity has has 2 passives. One sets Poison Zone on switch in and extends it."e\bThe other lowers the target's Attack or Sp. Attack if it's poisoned or paralyzed respectively."~\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Frenzied Sludge Wave. It can only be used if there's an opponent with a status condition."�\bIt can't be protected against, lowers the target's Sp. Defense by -2 and poisons it if it doesn't already have a status condition."^\bIngo's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. His Chandelure can Dynamax."�\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as increasing the power of its team's next special moves."�\bIt also has a B Move, Rising Flames Hex. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."�\bIt applies effects based on what the target's inflicted with:\nParalysis - Lower target's Defense by -2.\n Burn - Lower target's Sp. Defense by -2."^\bPoison - Heal itself and allies for a little HP.\n Flinch - Lower target's Speed by -2."b\bTrap - Power up user's next physical move.\n Confusion - Power up user's next special move."�\bEmmet's Trainer Move gives a Pokémon on his side Ground immunity for 5 turns and makes its next moves critical hits. His Eelektross can Dynamax."m\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as trapping the target."�\bIt also has a B Move, Descending Lightning Wild Charge. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"g\bSerena's Trainer Move gives her +6 Zygarde's Attack and Sp. Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."\\bZygarde's passives prevent its stats from being lowered and its attacks from missing."p\bLastly, it also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move gives her Marshadow +4 Attack and +3 Speed and Evasion. After attacking, Marshadow's passive raises one of its stats by +1 3 times."|\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Sp. Defense by the same amount of stages."`\bThen, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."x\bDiancie's B Move, Pink Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up."M\bIt lowers the target's Defense by -2 while giving its side +2 Defense."�\bDiancie's passives lower all opponents' Speed by -1 when entering battle and Mega Evolving, as well as giving it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate after using a move."_\bLysandre's Trainer Move gives his +4 Volcanion Sp. Attack, +1 Accuracy and +3 Crit Rate."�\bVolcanion itself has one passive which burns the targets that it hits. This is then complimented with its B Move, Heat Hydro Pump."�\bIt can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned and is an AoE move which deals more damage to burned targets."o\bThen, based on how many burned targets it hits, it makes Volcanion's next special attack do more damage."I\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana, Acerola,Mina,Gladion]"v\bLusamine's Trainer Move gives Necrozma +6 Sp. Attack and -1 Speed. Her Dusk-Mane Necrozma can also Ultra Burst."�\bIt also has passives which turns its single target moves into AoE moves and allows Prismatic Laser to be used without the user recharging."M\bHau's Trainer Move gives his Tapu Koko +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."z\bWhen entering battle, one of Koko's passives extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next special attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."l\bThen, Koko's B Move, Wild Electroweb, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the Speed of all targets by -2 while +2 Speed to Koko and its allies."H\bLana's Trainer Move gives her Tapu Lele +6 Attack and Sp. Attack."y\bWhen entering battle, one of Lele's passives extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up its next physical and special attacks when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."{\bLastly, its B Move, Neo Psycho Cut, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move gives +2 Defense and +3 Crit Rate to her side's Pokémon. If it's Sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), it gives +2 Attack too."v\bWhen entering battle, Bulu's first passive extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next physical attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."t\bLastly, its B Move, Unbreakable Swords Dance, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."b\bIt gives +2 Attack to Bulu and its allies makes their next physical attacks do more damage."�\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side and gives +4 Sp. Attack (+6 if Raining) and Gradual Healing to the Pokémon on her side."x\bWhen entering battle, Tapu Fini's ability sets Fairy Zone (because Misty Terrain sucks) and extends its duration."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which gives its side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."p\bLastly, Fini's B Move, Sea Deity Protect, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt applies Protect to itself and its allies, then it restores 20% HP (30% with Fairy Zone) for itself and its allies and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's Raining."q\bGladion's Trainer Move gives his Magearna +6 Sp. Attack, +3 Crit Rate and powers up its next special move."�\bMagearna has passives which lower the target's Sp. Attack by -2 after using a move and prevent its own stats from being lowered."]\bThen, Magearna's B Move, Piercing Fleur Cannon, can only be used after it uses a move."}\bIts power and the power of its next special move increases based on how much the targets' Sp. Attack has been lowered.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon,Piers,Gloria (Dojo)]"o\bLeon's Trainer Move gives his Eternatus +3 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate but lowers its Sp. Defense by -1."�\bHis Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and one of its passives enables its Eternabeam to not require a recharge turn after it's used."~\bIts other passive also lowers the target's Attack, Defense, Sp. Attack, Sp. Defense, Speed, Accuracy and Evasion by -1."O\bPier's Trainer Move gives his Toxtricity +2 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."�\bToxtricity has passives which set Electric Terrain and extend it on switch in, as well as ignore the target's enduring effects."}\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Sorrowful Echos Overdrive. It can only be used if there's an active weather, terrain or zone."�\bIt also can't be protected against and does more damage if the target has a status condition, which would most likely happen from its Sludge Bomb."Z\bGloria's Trainer Move gives her Urshifu +3 Attack. Her Urshifu can also Gigantamax."p\bOther than that, it just has passives which lower the target's Defense and Speed by -1 when hitting them."j\bWith Surging Strikes, it'll apply to each hit, so you'll actually end up with -3 Defense and Speed!"v\bNice choice! These guys were made for PoMas's anniversaries and are much simpler compared to the Neo Champions."m\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lillie (2022),N (2022),Steven (2022), May (2023),Skyla (2023),Raihan (2023)]"l\bFun fact: This is my favourite anniversary trainer out of them all! Her skirt is sooo good... anyway!"m\bLillie's Trainer Move gives her Lunala +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, the first of its kind in PoMas."b\bIts passives set Tailwind when its switched in and powers up its moves when its HP is full."r\bN's Trainer Move gives his Reshiram +3 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy, as well as setting Tailwind on his side."v\bIts passives turn its single target moves into AoE moves and lower the target's Sp. Defense after attacking it."K\bSteven's Trainer Move gives his Rayquaza +2 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."a\bIts passives turn stat drops into stat increases and gives it +1 Speed after using a move."{\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Latias +2 Defense and Sp. Defense and +3 Crit Rate, as well as setting Tailwind on her side."s\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and doubles stat drops that it inflicts."s\bSkyla's Trainer Move gives her Tornadus +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as giving her side +2 Speed."v\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and confuses the target after attacking it."�\bRaihan's Trainer Move gives his Flygon +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate, then powers up his team's next physical and special moves."�\bIts passives power up its team's next physical and special moves when using a status move and when attacking a target that's flinching, trapped or confused, it lowers its attacking stats by -1."&\bLastly, his Flygon can Dynamax."n\bHoho! All of these guys have a Master Passive (I'm assuming you know what that is by now) and a B Move."y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Calem,Marnie, Hop,Bede,Red,Leaf,Blue,Nate,Rosa,Silver,Cheren, Bianca,May,Brendan]"w\bSerena has quite a lot going on, so let's split her kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"n\bSerena is quite interesting. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."\bThe simplest part of her kit is definitely her Trainer Move. It gives her Greninja +2 Attack, +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."5\bHer Greninja also has a Spirit Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which max out the number of hits of a multi-strike move and for each hit, it lowers a random stat of the target by -1."T\bThat means its Water Shuriken will always end up lowering your stats 5 times!"z\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which lower the target's Accuracy by -1 and has a chance of making it flinch."b\bBoundless Quick Attack won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"�\bIt makes the target weaker to Greninja's current type, as well as lower its Defense and Sp. Defense by -2 and give its side +3 Speed."v\bCalem has quite a lot going on, so let's split his kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"g\bCalem is pretty cool. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."�\bThe simplest part of his kit is definitely his Trainer Move. It gives his side +4 Attack, +2 Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, then sets up Tailwind."4\bHis Greninja also has a Pride Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to status conditions, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in the rain."�\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to stat drops, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in a Dark Zone."h\bTransformational Double Team won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"c\bWhen Greninja's a Water type, it'll make it rain and power up its side's next special moves."i\bIf it's a Dark type, it'll set up a Dark Zone and power up its side's next physical moves instead."S\bThen regardless of type, it'll also give Greninja and its allies +2 Evasion."�\bMarnie's Trainer Move gives her Galarian Moltres +6 Sp. Attack, +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. It then takes 10% of its max HP as recoil damage."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives give it +3 Crit Rate when switching in and powers up its moves when it's not at max HP."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fierce Fiery Wrath, can only be used after 2 other moves have been used. It can't be protected against and flinchest its target(s)."q\bHop's Trainer Move gives his Galarian Zapdos +3 Speed and -1 Sp. Defense. It then sets up a Fighting Zone."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives give it +2 Attack on entry and lower the target's Sp. Defense when lowering its Defense."�\bLastly, its B Move, Roaring Thunderous Kick, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It lowers the target's Defense by -3."�\bBede's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Attack, Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, as well as powering up his side's next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives give its side +1 Speed on entry and makes it immune to critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Intimidating Freezing Glare, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It gives his side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."i\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Kantonian Articuno +6 Sp. Attack and powers up its next special move."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, it has quite a few other passives. First off, its moves will always land and be critical hits."�\bThen, it lowers its target's resistance to ice moves and powers up its next special attack based on how many opponents its move hit."�\bLastly, its B Move, Frozen Wings Ice Beam, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type and freezes the target."a\bLeaf's Trainer Move gives her Kantonian Moltres +6 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."Z\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its passives supercharge its status moves."�\bIn addition to their original effects, it makes them lower the target's Attack, Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense by -1 and makes it weaker to Fire moves."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fiery Wings Flare Blitz, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type. It burns the target and double its stat drops."z\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as powering up their next special moves."^\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its passives make its moves very potent."�\bIn addition to their original effects, they make the target weaker to Electric moves and give Zapdos's side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."r\bLastly, its B Move, Thundering Wings Roost, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type."�\bIt heals Zapdos and its allies for 60% and 30% of their respective max HPs, gives its side Gradual Healing and removes all their status conditions."d\bNate's Trainer Move returns his Haxorus's lowered stats back to normal and gives it +3 Speed."~\bWith Nate using his Trainer Move, one of Haxorus's passives will also give it +6 Attack and power up its next physical move."`\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passive makes its moves critical hits."f\bLastly, its B Move, Dark Black Outrage, can only be used when Haxorus's Attack has been raised."�\bRosa's Trainer Move gives her side a boost to her team's special or physical moves when Meloetta is in its Aria or Pirouette forms respectively."}\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives play around the fact that Meloetta has 2 different forms."U\bFirst off, its Normal moves become the same type as Meloetta's secondary type."�\bAfter using a move, it then give its side +1 Defense or Sp. Defense (Pirouette and Aria respectively) and makes its target weaker to Meloetta's second type."p\bLastly, its B Move, Relic Song of Wonder, can only be used when Meloetta is at 1/3 or more of its max HP."�\bIt changes Meloetta's form and powers up its side's next physical and special moves and has a chance to make the target fall asleep."{\bSilver's Trainer Move gives his Tyranitar +6 Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as +1 Accuracy if used in a Sandstorm."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives strengthen it in a Sandstorm. First, it extends the duration of Sandstorms."\bIts moves also get powered up in a Sandstorm and it also gets a boost to its next physical attack after using an attack."�\bLastly, its B Move, Massive Rock Slide, always flinches its target(s) but can't be used consecutively or on Ttar's first turn in battle."�\bCheren's Trainer Move gives his Tornadus +4 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as powering it its next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives make its moves always land, be critical hits, then strengthen its next physical and special moves."y\bLastly, its B Move, Black Gale Bleakwind Storm, can't be used consecutively or on Tornadus's first turn in battle."}\bIt increases in power based on how much its next physical move would be powered up and lower the target's Speed by -2."}\bIn addition, if it's used as Tornadus's 2nd move after entering battle, it makes the target(s) weaker to Flying moves."K\bBianca's Trainer Move gives her Virizion +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives allow gives its side +1 Speed and Evasion after using a move and ignore enduring."�\bLastly, its B Move, White Light Sacred Sword, lowers the target's attacking stats by -3 and makes its weaker to Fighting moves."A\bIt also ignores the target's defensive and evasive boosts."�\bMay's Trainer Move powers up the next special move of a Pokémon on her side and her Kyogre, as well as giving the latter +2 Sp. Attack."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Sp. Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Blue Origin Pulse, can only be used in Heavy Rain. It lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Sp. Defense by -3."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move powers up the next physical move of a Pokémon on his side and his Groudon, as well as giving the latter +2 Attack."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."v\bLastly, its B Move, Red Precipice Blades, lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Defense by -2."v\bHowever, it can only be used in Harsh Sun and can't be used consecutively or on Groudon's first turn in battle."z\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bEssentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are 5 types of buffs: Blessings, Immunities, Restoration, Boosters and Crushers."q\bWhat buff type would you like to know about? \ch[1,-1,Blessings,Immunities,Restoration,Boosters, Crushers]"\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat increases at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level."�\bIn addition, you can buy an enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assasin's Blessing) for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bAs an example, Warrior's Blessing Lv. 1 will give your Pokémon +1 Attack when they enter battle, essentially giving them Intrepid Sword!"�\bImmunites make your Pokémon immune to status conditions, "interferences" (i.e. flinching, trapping and confusion) or even critical hits for some time."Q\bAll of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."�\bHowever, once you buy out the whole store, you can then buy buffs that make you immune to all status conditions and interferences."<\bThey will use up 4 and 3 energy respectively, though."�\bIf you talk to Nurse Joy now, she'll actually heal your team now! But... just a little bit, if you don't give her any energy. Better than nothing though, amirite?"�\bAt base, she'll heal your team for 10% of its HP, as well as restore 1/8 of its PP (restoring at least 1 PP per move, though)."�\bThe restoration buffs increase those amounts though. For each level of the HP Recovery buff, she'll heal 25%, 50% and 100% of your team's HP."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your 'mons alive!"m\bFor each level of the PP Recovery buff, it'll restore 1/4, 1/2 and all of your team's PP respectively."�\bFurthermore, she also won't remove status conditions from your team; you'll have to equip the Status Recovery buff first! It costs 3 energy."�\bLastly, these buffs are only active in the Sync Challenge. If she gave any healing in the Titan Challenge, it would be wayyy too easy!"}\bBoosters give your Pokémon +1 to a stat (except Accuracy and Evasion) after they use a move, even if the move failed."Q\bAll of them use 1 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."l\bCrushers lowers one of the target's stats (except Accuracy and Evasion) by -1 after they're attacked."f\bAlso, they won't be effective in Titan Challenge; all opponents there are immune to stat drops."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."R\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Get ready and take care now!"L\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."]\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold. An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."r\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision. This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"Y\bHey, partner! Can I interest you in some moves? They don't have these anywhere else, you know.\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas,Dual Wingbeat, Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam,Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage, Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]" \bCome again! Or not. Hehe."\bAny other moves?\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas, Dual Wingbeat,Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam, Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage,Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now. Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here? You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations! So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"s\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players. Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"Z\bAlright, you got so far! What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players. I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"U\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand. Sheesh. :)"^\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it. Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."T\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"|\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Galar,Hisui,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rAwwww, be careful out there. *wink*"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs</i>. <i>Sobs</i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bIn this challenge specifically, you also won't be able to inflict your opponents with status conditions, flinch, trap or confuse them!"�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"{\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Titan Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your mons alive!"i\bAlso, they won't be effective here in the Titan Challenge; all opponents are immune to stat drops."!\bFoul: Why hello there pal!"\bAre you lost?"�\bTook the wrong turn looking for the bathroom? Well don't you worry, just follow me and I will take you back to where you're supposed to be."9\bOh who am I kidding. We both know you're not lost."f\bThis is one of the most secure facilities in this dimension; people don't just get "lost" here."t\bYour luck seems to have run out now that I've found you before the other two, see, I'm not as nice as them..."!\bBut then again, I'm bored."\bEhhh, why not."~\bSee, it would be mean if I defeated you now, but wouldn't it be even meaner if I healed you, just to make you wipe out?"+\bLet me show you what I mean by that!"<\bNot too bad, maybe you do have some skills after all."L\bNow scram and make sure I don't catch you sneaking around here again!"d\bBut maybe leave a resume on your way out. We might need someone of your talent in the future."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."K\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round..."0\r*sighs* I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."v\rVermint: Hello \PN, I hope you enjoy your stay here. Try not to think too much about our first encounter, okay?"W\rVermint: Hello \PN, I had foreseen that I would have to introduce myself to you."^\rMy true name is Vera. I created your wardrobe and I am also here to judge your resolve."-\rI hope this isn't a shock to you, \PN."bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."JYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"FAn ominous Vending Machine stares at you. Best not to go near it."=PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS ENEMY SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"vYou can't seem to get the Vending Machine to work anymore. Maybe it can only be used before starting a challenge?"#The exit seems to be locked..."?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"c\bLuc-ker: Oh, you want to battle me at my full power? Fine, but don't say you weren't warned."G\bLuc: Too easy, huh? I lied - that wasn't actually my full power."�\bMy real master, Yhwach, gifted me with the shift V - The Visionary, turning my imagination into reality! That means I can throw at you whatever I can conjure and I simply haven't had enough to imagine yet."\bUntil next time!"Z\bLuc: Hehe, that's a taste of what's to come soon. Thanks for letting me go all-out!"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then."C\rDid you know that there's a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."�\rHow do you know if you're strong? I heard another rumour that, if you get good in Club, and I mean <i>real good</i> in Club, they'll acknowledge you."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"^\rHuh? You don't know what I'm talking about? Hahaha, you haven't lost to them, have you?"X\rYou're either really good, or you haven't been whooped yet. Either way, have fun!"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."1\ch[98,-1,Display your Staff Pass,Walk Away]"b\bOh, you are one of the staff here? You should have show me your pass earlier. Please enter."\bPlease leave. Thank you."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"P\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your original bag back soon enough.">\bYou have a Backstage Pass. Let me tear that up for you."R\bHow strange. You don't seem to have a backstage pass. Try buying one again." \bPlease let me escort you."�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"T\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you, \PN! (The hyphen is important by the way.)"�\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics. By the way, you can call me Luc for short if my full name is too hard for you."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"~\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Finish]"W\bThe Club Challenge - here, you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"w\bYou'll be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle. If you do well enough, you might get some... *ahem* privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no items, so it's a good place to grind your Pokémon!"}\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, the challenge that chucks trainers at you until your team drops (or until you defeat 150 trainers)."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."�\bYour longest, most glorious run will be logged for you so you can boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"x\bThe Mayhem Challenge - in this one, you battle with trainers in a full battles and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's because they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You'll never know what's up their sleeves!"^\bThey have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge; you'll battle "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge you'll be battling Sync Pokémon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."|YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION.\ch[98,-1,View active buffs,Other options?,Close menu]"iThe other options have been grayed out. Maybe they can only be accessed before starting a challenge?"\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b40 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!"2\b\v[61] GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same.".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?"9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day."e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."]\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE. Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?"*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL OFFER DEAL***, Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits), Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems (1 Credit), Held Items,Credit-Money Exchange]"o\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits), VIP Backstage Pass (5 Credits), Grandeur Club Staff Pass (500 Credits)]"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME.""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"0BACKSTAGE PASS NOT FOR SALE YET! THANK YOU!".BACKSTAGE PASS ALREADY BOUGHT! THANK YOU!"7YOU ALREADY OWN A STAFF PASS. COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"WLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Master"Challenge"Win Counts"Cancel"Backstage"	Yes?"No![�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!".\rWould you like to recieve some healing?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"o\rCan't believe you made me fully restore your team, you bastard. This wasn't supposed to even be a thing."`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."9\rYour team should already be at full health, right?"8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto, Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary, Neo Champion,Sygna Buffs]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto, Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary,Neo Champion]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."�\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying! That is, if you don't hit F12 because you're a sore loser or a tryhard."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bThey'll also have some interesting moves too, ranging from moves used by their trainers instead or powerful moves that can only be used under certain conditions."�\bFuthermore, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"�\bBut lastly, and you might find a silver lining in this - I've made it so that not only do you benefit from some damage reduction, the "harder" trainers have a lower chance to show up early."�\bSo if you want to familiarise yourself with the trainers here, it might be good to try this challenge with a lower difficulty first.".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure. Which one would you like me to explain? \ch[1,-1,Crit Rate,Trainer Move,B Move,Passive Skill, Master Passive,Zone,Gradual Healing]"R\bCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages."�\bTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses (rather than their Pokémon). These moves tend to buff the user's Pokémon or their team's side."^\bThey can be used even when the trainer's Pokémon is afflicted with a status condition."}\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. You can identify them by the "descriptor" in the move's name, e.g. Origin Volt Tackle."~\bThey tend to do what the move they're based on does, but with increased power, added effects or the regular effect enhanced."\bThere's usually a condition that has to be met before each B Move can be used, so use that to your advantage to counter them!"�\bIf they don't, they will likely have very little PP instead. Lastly, all trainers only have 1 B Move at most, but there is 1 exception."mPassive Skill - Essentially an extra ability, but they can't be ignored by effects such as Mold Breaker."~\bHow many a Pokémon has is completely arbitrary, though I've tried to limit it to 3 at most, excluding Master Passives."l\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the team's damage dealt and reduces the damage taken."k\bThere are 3 types: Flag Bearer is for all moves and is 10% damage increase and 20% damage reduction."W\bPride is for physical moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."_\bLastly, Spirit is for special moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."`\bZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type by 50%."s\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn. Think of it kinda like Leftovers."T\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika, Red,Red (Thunderbolt),Blue,Leaf]"W\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit."�\bAnyway, his Trainer Move give his Tyranitar's +1 Defense and makes its next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but there are ways to get around it, like Protect."�\bTtar has 2 passives. One gives its moves a higher chance to apply their additional effects and the other prevents its stats from dropping in a sandstorm."s\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move gives her Vaporeon +2 Defense and her side +2 Sp. Defense."�\bLastly, her Vaporeon's passives give it gradual healing when switching in as well as a chance to raise its Evasion after it uses a move."}\bErika's Trainer Move gives her Leafeon's +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, but if the Sun's up, these stat increases are doubled."`\bLeafeon's ability is Chorophyll, so with the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled."t\bThen, its passives don't allow status conditions to be inflicted on it as well as heal it after using a move."@\bIn other words, you really don't want Leafeon in the Sun!"�\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Charizard's +3 Attack, Sp. Attack and Speed and +2 Crit Rate, though its Defense and Sp. Defense are lowered by -1."{\bHis Charizard also has passives which allow its moves to never miss and not require a rechage turn after using them."X\bKnow what that means? It's able to use Blast Burn. Every. Single. Turn. Have fun!"s\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move gives Pikachu +6 Attack and Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since there you only use 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair per battle."h\bIt also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."{\bIts other passives make all its moves critical hits, as well as healing it after it uses a move in Electric Terrain."q\bLast, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a B Move which can only be used when Electric Terrain's active."X\bIf your Pokémon's paralyzed, its Defense and Sp. Defense are also lowered by -1."r\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Defense and +1 Crit Rate, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."~\bAnyway, his Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, one of its passive gives his side +1 Attack and Sp. Attack."�\bAnd then when it attacks, its other passive gives its side +1 Sp. Defense. Lastly, it also doesn't need to recharge after using Hydro Cannon."`\bWith Leaf's Trainer Move, I took a few creative liberties to make it live up to its name."q\bIt provides the Pokémon on her side Gradual Healing, as well as healing them all for 40% of their max HP!"�\bAs for Venusaur's passives, they badly poison your Pokémon and gives them -1 to their defensive stats after they're attacked by it."h\bWith Razor Leaf and a non-recharging Frenzy Plant, it's sure to deal out a ton poison and damage."Y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris, Silver,Giovanni,Giovanni (Ultra)]"q\bMorty's Trainer Move gives +1 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate to his side, as well as setting Tailwind."�\bOne of Ho-oh's passives gives additional stat boosts to its team if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."a\bIts other passive then heals the Pokémon on Ho- oh's side when it uses a move in the Sun."s\bEthan's Trainer Move powers up Lugia's next special move, gives it +1 Accuracy and makes its next move crit."{\bLugia has passives which makes its single target attacks hit all opponents as well as restore PP to Ethan's Trainer Move."k\bLastly, it also has a Spirit Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bLyra's Trainer Move gives +2 Attack and Sp. Attack to a Pokémon on her side and gives them Gradual Healing. But that's not the crazy thing about this sync pair."�\bCelebi has passives which leaves the opponent flinched, trapped and confused after using a move and lowers one of the target's stats by -2."v\bAnnnnd Celebi has Grassy Glide and can set up Grassy Terrain too to give it priority. Talk about a nasty combo!"j\bLastly, it also has a Pride Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."N\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers."O\bAt base, her Trainer Move gives her side +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate."{\bBut if it's Raining, it also powers up the next special attack from her team, making them pack an even bigger punch."�\bOne of Suicune's passives gives its side +4 Sp. Defense if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."�\bIts other passive heals its team after a uses a move under the Rain. I think you get the idea - Rain is dangerous if you're facing Kris!"k\bLastly, it has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."k\bSilver's Trainer Move gives Sneasel +3 Attack and Speed, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."�\bSneasel's B Move, Crushing Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. In theory, that doesn't sound too hard to counter, right?"\bWell, on every hit of a multi-hit move, its passives lower the opposing Pokémon's Speed by -1 while it gets +1 Evasion."~\bIt also gets +1 Crit Rate on each hit of its B Move too, but it doesn't have any other ways of increasing its damage itself."N\bSo at best, you get lucky and OHKO it, while at worst, it's a nuisance."<\bGiovanni's Trainer Move gives his Nidoking +6 Attack."a\bHis Nidoking has a passive to make all its attacks critical hits, including its Max Moves."�\bIts other passive turns Normal moves into Ground moves, allowing it to gain STAB from it. Its Mega Kick is going to hit pretty hard!"�\bThis version of Giovanni has a Trainer Move which gives his side +2 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as making Guzzlord the center of attention."{\bGuzzlord has passives which enable its Stockpile Defense and Sp. Defense boosts to be tripled and shared with its allies."O\bHowever, it can only Stockpile a maximum of 2 times as a result of this."�\bGuzzlord also doesn't have just 1 B Move, but 2! It's the one exception to the "rule" that says there can only be 1 B Move for each sync pair."i\bWhen used, they both remove Stockpiles's stat boosts and restores 1 PP to Giovanni's Trainer Move."�\bThe first one, Guzzling Swallow, can only be used after Stockpile has been used and restores Guzzlord's HP based on how many times it was used."=\bThen, it restores a fixed amount of HP for its allies."�\bThe second one is Gourging Crunch. It can only be used when the Guzzlord's stat boosts for Defense and Sp. Defense are 6 or greater."9\bIt then lowers the target's defensive stats by -1.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Blaziken +4 Attack and +1 Accuracy, sets up Tailwind and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."�\bBlaziken's first passive gives +1 Speed to its side when entering battle, including Mega Evolution, effectively translating to a +2 increase."�\bIts other passive lowers the target's Defense by -2. All in all, very speedy and it can easily snowball if you're not careful."c\bBrendan's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense as well as +1 Crit Rate."u\bHis Latios's first passive powers up its sides' next special moves when entering the battle and Mega Evolving."x\bIts other passive then increases the likelihood of additional effects; if it's a stat drop, it'll be doubled too."p\bIt has Luster Purge, so that'll mean that you'll be taking a lot of special damage if you're not careful!"�\bSteven... is a lot. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4! So let's break him down a bit.\ch[2,-1,Initial State,Shared Traits, Normal Forme,Attack Forme,Defense Forme,Speed Forme]"\bInitially, Deoxys starts in its Normal Forme with 4 Trainer Moves and a passive which gives it +1 Accuracy when switching in."�\bThe first one, "Try This!", sets Psychic Terrain and gives Deoxys +2 Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed and keep Deoxys in its Normal Forme."u\bHis second one, "Attack!", gives Deoxys +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme."�\bThe third one, "Defend!" gives its +4 side Attack and Sp. Attack. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn."r\bLast but not least,"Faster!", gives Deoxys +6 Speed and +3 Evasion and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme."�\bOutside of its inital state, all forms of Deoxys that Steven has have a passive with converts stat drops into stat increases, but not vice versa like Contrary does!"a\bThey all also have Psycho Boost and Zen Headbutt, so I won't be mentioning them elsewhere."`\bIn its Normal Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."{\bIt also has a passive which increase the chance of additional effects, so if it uses Zen Headbutt, be prepared to flinch!"`\bIn its Attack Forme, Deoxys has Protect and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which increases the power of its next physical and special moves, so it might quickly snowball out of control!"a\bIn its Defense Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Iron Defense in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which gives its side +2 Sp. Defense each time a status move is used, so with Iron Defense it'll become very bulky very quickly."^\bIn its Speed Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Double Team in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which sets up Tailwind for its side when a status move is successful the first time it's used in battle."_\bWally's Trainer Move gives his Gardevoir +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Sp. Defense and Crit Rate."�\bGardevoir has 2 passives - the first gives its side +1 Speed when entering battle and Mega Evolving; the other leaves the target confused after a move."�\bGardevoir also has a B Move, Ultimate Dazzling Gleam. It lowers the targets' Attack and Sp. Attack by -4, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks."�\bIt can only be used once, but you can't Protect against it and -4 on your attacking stats will likely force you to switch out your Pokémon."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."�\bApart from that, Kommo-o has passives which allow it to ignore damage reduction from Reflect, Light Screen and Aurora Veil as well as increase the chance for additional effects."�\bThis version of Cynthia's Trainer Move gives Giratina +4 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate. She can also set a Ghost Zone."T\bHer Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Sp. Defense of the target by -1."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move gives her side +4 Defense and Sp. Defense, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll give +6 instead."r\bAs for that, her Lucario has a passive which sets Fighting Zone on entry, so most of the time, it'll be +6."s\bLucario's other passive also depends on Fighting Zone - it heals its side after using a move if it's active."y\bIt also has Superior Aura Sphere, a B Move that never misses and can only be used after Lucario is attacked twice."]\bAfter it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of its side."p\bLastly, Lucario has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."\bCyrus's Trainer Move gives his Darkrai +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy and Crit Rate. In addition, he can set a Dark Zone."�\bDarkrai has passives which power up its moves if the target is asleep, or if it's using a status move, it'll lower a random stat of all opponents by -1."[\bIt does have Dark Void, but even if it misses, its 2nd passive will activate anyway."�\bDawn's Trainer Move gives her side +2 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP."^\bYou might be thinking, why do that, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"i\bCresselia's very tanky, but one of its passives makes it even more so when it has 50% HP or lower."�\bIts other passive also increases the power of its side's special moves if Cresselia uses a status move when it's HP is 50% or lower."P\bIt also has Moonlight for healing, so don't count your chickens too soon!"R\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N, Roxie,Ingo,Emmet]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move gives +2 Accuracy and Crit Rate to a Pokémon on her side, as well as giving +2 Sp. Attack to all Pokémon on her side."�\bRotom has a passive which gives it +1 Evasion when it's hit, as well as another which prevents its Evasion from being lowered."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it gives +6 Attack and Evasion and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition, it has passives which increase the chance of the additional effects its moves and increase their power when Sharpedo is in a pinch."s\bHilbert's Trainer Move gives his Genesect +3 Sp. Attack, +2 Crit Rate and powers up its next special attack."�\bWhen using Techno Blast, Genesect changes form depending on the type the target is weakest to. Its default is also Bug instead of Normal."]\bThen, it makes them weaker to that type and applies an effect corresponding that type."m\bElectric - Paralyze target.\n Fire - Lower target's Attack by -1.\n Ice - 50% chance to freeze target."H\bWater - Lower target's Defense by -1. Bug - No additional effect."d\bLastly, if Genesect lands a super effective hit, its passive lowers the target's Speed by -2."�\bHilda's Trainer Move raises her Victini's Sp. Attack by how much its Attack has been raised, then gives it +3 Crit Rate and gives its team +1 Accuracy."�\bThis is complemented by Victini's passives, which gives it +2 Attack on switching in and turns stat drops into stat increases."y\bThere's even more synergy - Victini has V-Create, so it just keeps getting bulkier and faster each time it's used!"D\bN's Trainer Move gives his Kyurem +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bWhen Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it has a passive which halves the damage it takes while charging and unlocks its B Move, Resonating Noble Roar."|\bIt lowers the Attack, Sp. Attack, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by -2, while it powering up its next physical attack."�\bFreeze Shock then needs to be used again before it can be used again, preventing it from being spammed endlessly (it also has 3 PP)."�\bKyurem also has a passive which allows it to ignore the opponent's enduring effects, but I imagine that won't come up too often."q\bRoxie's Trainer Move gives her Toxtricity +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate and applies Tailwind to her side."W\bToxtricity has has 2 passives. One sets Poison Zone on switch in and extends it."e\bThe other lowers the target's Attack or Sp. Attack if it's poisoned or paralyzed respectively."~\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Frenzied Sludge Wave. It can only be used if there's an opponent with a status condition."�\bIt can't be protected against, lowers the target's Sp. Defense by -2 and poisons it if it doesn't already have a status condition."^\bIngo's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. His Chandelure can Dynamax."�\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as increasing the power of its team's next special moves."�\bIt also has a B Move, Rising Flames Hex. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."�\bIt applies effects based on what the target's inflicted with:\nParalysis - Lower target's Defense by -2.\n Burn - Lower target's Sp. Defense by -2."^\bPoison - Heal itself and allies for a little HP.\n Flinch - Lower target's Speed by -2."b\bTrap - Power up user's next physical move.\n Confusion - Power up user's next special move."�\bEmmet's Trainer Move gives a Pokémon on his side Ground immunity for 5 turns and makes its next moves critical hits. His Eelektross can Dynamax."m\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as trapping the target."�\bIt also has a B Move, Descending Lightning Wild Charge. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"g\bSerena's Trainer Move gives her +6 Zygarde's Attack and Sp. Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."\\bZygarde's passives prevent its stats from being lowered and its attacks from missing."p\bLastly, it also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move gives her Marshadow +4 Attack and +3 Speed and Evasion. After attacking, Marshadow's passive raises one of its stats by +1 3 times."|\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Sp. Defense by the same amount of stages."`\bThen, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."x\bDiancie's B Move, Pink Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up."M\bIt lowers the target's Defense by -2 while giving its side +2 Defense."�\bDiancie's passives lower all opponents' Speed by -1 when entering battle and Mega Evolving, as well as giving it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate after using a move."_\bLysandre's Trainer Move gives his +4 Volcanion Sp. Attack, +1 Accuracy and +3 Crit Rate."�\bVolcanion itself has one passive which burns the targets that it hits. This is then complimented with its B Move, Heat Hydro Pump."�\bIt can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned and is an AoE move which deals more damage to burned targets."o\bThen, based on how many burned targets it hits, it makes Volcanion's next special attack do more damage."I\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana, Acerola,Mina,Gladion]"v\bLusamine's Trainer Move gives Necrozma +6 Sp. Attack and -1 Speed. Her Dusk-Mane Necrozma can also Ultra Burst."�\bIt also has passives which turns its single target moves into AoE moves and allows Prismatic Laser to be used without the user recharging."M\bHau's Trainer Move gives his Tapu Koko +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."z\bWhen entering battle, one of Koko's passives extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next special attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."l\bThen, Koko's B Move, Wild Electroweb, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the Speed of all targets by -2 while +2 Speed to Koko and its allies."H\bLana's Trainer Move gives her Tapu Lele +6 Attack and Sp. Attack."y\bWhen entering battle, one of Lele's passives extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up its next physical and special attacks when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."{\bLastly, its B Move, Neo Psycho Cut, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move gives +2 Defense and +3 Crit Rate to her side's Pokémon. If it's Sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), it gives +2 Attack too."v\bWhen entering battle, Bulu's first passive extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next physical attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."t\bLastly, its B Move, Unbreakable Swords Dance, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."b\bIt gives +2 Attack to Bulu and its allies makes their next physical attacks do more damage."�\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side and gives +4 Sp. Attack (+6 if Raining) and Gradual Healing to the Pokémon on her side."x\bWhen entering battle, Tapu Fini's ability sets Fairy Zone (because Misty Terrain sucks) and extends its duration."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which gives its side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."p\bLastly, Fini's B Move, Sea Deity Protect, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt applies Protect to itself and its allies, then it restores 20% HP (30% with Fairy Zone) for itself and its allies and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's Raining."q\bGladion's Trainer Move gives his Magearna +6 Sp. Attack, +3 Crit Rate and powers up its next special move."�\bMagearna has passives which lower the target's Sp. Attack by -2 after using a move and prevent its own stats from being lowered."]\bThen, Magearna's B Move, Piercing Fleur Cannon, can only be used after it uses a move."}\bIts power and the power of its next special move increases based on how much the targets' Sp. Attack has been lowered.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon,Piers,Gloria (Dojo)]"o\bLeon's Trainer Move gives his Eternatus +3 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate but lowers its Sp. Defense by -1."�\bHis Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and one of its passives enables its Eternabeam to not require a recharge turn after it's used."~\bIts other passive also lowers the target's Attack, Defense, Sp. Attack, Sp. Defense, Speed, Accuracy and Evasion by -1."O\bPier's Trainer Move gives his Toxtricity +2 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."�\bToxtricity has passives which set Electric Terrain and extend it on switch in, as well as ignore the target's enduring effects."}\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Sorrowful Echos Overdrive. It can only be used if there's an active weather, terrain or zone."�\bIt also can't be protected against and does more damage if the target has a status condition, which would most likely happen from its Sludge Bomb."Z\bGloria's Trainer Move gives her Urshifu +3 Attack. Her Urshifu can also Gigantamax."p\bOther than that, it just has passives which lower the target's Defense and Speed by -1 when hitting them."j\bWith Surging Strikes, it'll apply to each hit, so you'll actually end up with -3 Defense and Speed!"v\bNice choice! These guys were made for PoMas's anniversaries and are much simpler compared to the Neo Champions."m\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lillie (2022),N (2022),Steven (2022), May (2023),Skyla (2023),Raihan (2023)]"l\bFun fact: This is my favourite anniversary trainer out of them all! Her skirt is sooo good... anyway!"m\bLillie's Trainer Move gives her Lunala +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, the first of its kind in PoMas."b\bIts passives set Tailwind when its switched in and powers up its moves when its HP is full."r\bN's Trainer Move gives his Reshiram +3 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy, as well as setting Tailwind on his side."v\bIts passives turn its single target moves into AoE moves and lower the target's Sp. Defense after attacking it."K\bSteven's Trainer Move gives his Rayquaza +2 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."a\bIts passives turn stat drops into stat increases and gives it +1 Speed after using a move."{\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Latias +2 Defense and Sp. Defense and +3 Crit Rate, as well as setting Tailwind on her side."s\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and doubles stat drops that it inflicts."s\bSkyla's Trainer Move gives her Tornadus +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as giving her side +2 Speed."v\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and confuses the target after attacking it."�\bRaihan's Trainer Move gives his Flygon +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate, then powers up his team's next physical and special moves."�\bIts passives power up its team's next physical and special moves when using a status move and when attacking a target that's flinching, trapped or confused, it lowers its attacking stats by -1."&\bLastly, his Flygon can Dynamax."n\bHoho! All of these guys have a Master Passive (I'm assuming you know what that is by now) and a B Move."y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Calem,Marnie, Hop,Bede,Red,Leaf,Blue,Nate,Rosa,Silver,Cheren, Bianca,May,Brendan]"w\bSerena has quite a lot going on, so let's split her kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"n\bSerena is quite interesting. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."\bThe simplest part of her kit is definitely her Trainer Move. It gives her Greninja +2 Attack, +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."5\bHer Greninja also has a Spirit Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which max out the number of hits of a multi-strike move and for each hit, it lowers a random stat of the target by -1."T\bThat means its Water Shuriken will always end up lowering your stats 5 times!"z\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which lower the target's Accuracy by -1 and has a chance of making it flinch."b\bBoundless Quick Attack won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"�\bIt makes the target weaker to Greninja's current type, as well as lower its Defense and Sp. Defense by -2 and give its side +3 Speed."v\bCalem has quite a lot going on, so let's split his kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"g\bCalem is pretty cool. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."�\bThe simplest part of his kit is definitely his Trainer Move. It gives his side +4 Attack, +2 Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, then sets up Tailwind."4\bHis Greninja also has a Pride Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to status conditions, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in the rain."�\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to stat drops, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in a Dark Zone."h\bTransformational Double Team won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"c\bWhen Greninja's a Water type, it'll make it rain and power up its side's next special moves."i\bIf it's a Dark type, it'll set up a Dark Zone and power up its side's next physical moves instead."S\bThen regardless of type, it'll also give Greninja and its allies +2 Evasion."�\bMarnie's Trainer Move gives her Galarian Moltres +6 Sp. Attack, +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. It then takes 10% of its max HP as recoil damage."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives give it +3 Crit Rate when switching in and powers up its moves when it's not at max HP."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fierce Fiery Wrath, can only be used after 2 other moves have been used. It can't be protected against and flinchest its target(s)."q\bHop's Trainer Move gives his Galarian Zapdos +3 Speed and -1 Sp. Defense. It then sets up a Fighting Zone."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives give it +2 Attack on entry and lower the target's Sp. Defense when lowering its Defense."�\bLastly, its B Move, Roaring Thunderous Kick, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It lowers the target's Defense by -3."�\bBede's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Attack, Sp.  Attack and Crit Rate, as well as powering up his side's next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives give its side +1 Speed on entry and makes it immune to critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Intimidating Freezing Glare, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It gives his side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."i\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Kantonian Articuno +6 Sp. Attack and powers up its next special move."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, it has quite a few other passives. First off, its moves will always land and be critical hits."�\bThen, it lowers its target's resistance to ice moves and powers up its next special attack based on how many opponents its move hit."�\bLastly, its B Move, Frozen Wings Ice Beam, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type and freezes the target."a\bLeaf's Trainer Move gives her Kantonian Moltres +6 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."Z\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its passives supercharge its status moves."�\bIn addition to their original effects, it makes them lower the target's Attack, Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense by -1 and makes it weaker to Fire moves."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fiery Wings Flare Blitz, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type. It burns the target and double its stat drops."z\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as powering up their next special moves."^\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its passives make its moves very potent."�\bIn addition to their original effects, they make the target weaker to Electric moves and give Zapdos's side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."r\bLastly, its B Move, Thundering Wings Roost, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type."�\bIt heals Zapdos and its allies for 60% and 30% of their respective max HPs, gives its side Gradual Healing and removes all their status conditions."d\bNate's Trainer Move returns his Haxorus's lowered stats back to normal and gives it +3 Speed."~\bWith Nate using his Trainer Move, one of Haxorus's passives will also give it +6 Attack and power up its next physical move."`\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passive makes its moves critical hits."f\bLastly, its B Move, Dark Black Outrage, can only be used when Haxorus's Attack has been raised."�\bRosa's Trainer Move gives her side a boost to her team's special or physical moves when Meloetta is in its Aria or Pirouette forms respectively."}\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives play around the fact that Meloetta has 2 different forms."U\bFirst off, its Normal moves become the same type as Meloetta's secondary type."�\bAfter using a move, it then give its side +1 Defense or Sp. Defense (Pirouette and Aria respectively) and makes its target weaker to Meloetta's second type."p\bLastly, its B Move, Relic Song of Wonder, can only be used when Meloetta is at 1/3 or more of its max HP."�\bIt changes Meloetta's form and powers up its side's next physical and special moves and has a chance to make the target fall asleep."{\bSilver's Trainer Move gives his Tyranitar +6 Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as +1 Accuracy if used in a Sandstorm."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives strengthen it in a Sandstorm. First, it extends the duration of Sandstorms."\bIts moves also get powered up in a Sandstorm and it also gets a boost to its next physical attack after using an attack."�\bLastly, its B Move, Massive Rock Slide, always flinches its target(s) but can't be used consecutively or on Ttar's first turn in battle."�\bCheren's Trainer Move gives his Tornadus +4 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as powering it its next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives make its moves always land, be critical hits, then strengthen its next physical and special moves."y\bLastly, its B Move, Black Gale Bleakwind Storm, can't be used consecutively or on Tornadus's first turn in battle."}\bIt increases in power based on how much its next physical move would be powered up and lower the target's Speed by -2."}\bIn addition, if it's used as Tornadus's 2nd move after entering battle, it makes the target(s) weaker to Flying moves."K\bBianca's Trainer Move gives her Virizion +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives allow gives its side +1 Speed and Evasion after using a move and ignore enduring."�\bLastly, its B Move, White Light Sacred Sword, lowers the target's attacking stats by -3 and makes its weaker to Fighting moves."A\bIt also ignores the target's defensive and evasive boosts."�\bMay's Trainer Move powers up the next special move of a Pokémon on her side and her Kyogre, as well as giving the latter +2 Sp. Attack."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Sp. Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Blue Origin Pulse, can only be used in Heavy Rain. It lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Sp. Defense by -3."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move powers up the next physical move of a Pokémon on his side and his Groudon, as well as giving the latter +2 Attack."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."v\bLastly, its B Move, Red Precipice Blades, lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Defense by -2."v\bHowever, it can only be used in Harsh Sun and can't be used consecutively or on Groudon's first turn in battle."z\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bEssentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs.  There are 5 types of buffs: Blessings, Immunities, Restoration, Boosters and Crushers."q\bWhat buff type would you like to know about? \ch[1,-1,Blessings,Immunities,Restoration,Boosters, Crushers]"\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat increases at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level."�\bIn addition, you can buy an enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assasin's Blessing) for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bAs an example, Warrior's Blessing Lv. 1 will give your Pokémon +1 Attack when they enter battle, essentially giving them Intrepid Sword!"�\bImmunites make your Pokémon immune to status conditions, "interferences" (i.e. flinching, trapping and confusion) or even critical hits for some time."Q\bAll of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."�\bHowever, once you buy out the whole store, you can then buy buffs that make you immune to all status conditions and interferences."<\bThey will use up 4 and 3 energy respectively, though."�\bIf you talk to Nurse Joy now, she'll actually heal your team now! But... just a little bit, if you don't give her any energy. Better than nothing though, amirite?"�\bAt base, she'll heal your team for 10% of its HP, as well as restore 1/8 of its PP (restoring at least 1 PP per move, though)."�\bThe restoration buffs increase those amounts though. For each level of the HP Recovery buff, she'll heal 25%, 50% and 100% of your team's HP."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your 'mons alive!"m\bFor each level of the PP Recovery buff, it'll restore 1/4, 1/2 and all of your team's PP respectively."�\bFurthermore, she also won't remove status conditions from your team; you'll have to equip the Status Recovery buff first! It costs 3 energy."�\bLastly, these buffs are only active in the Sync Challenge. If she gave any healing in the Titan Challenge, it would be wayyy too easy!"}\bBoosters give your Pokémon +1 to a stat (except Accuracy and Evasion) after they use a move, even if the move failed."Q\bAll of them use 1 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."l\bCrushers lowers one of the target's stats (except Accuracy and Evasion) by -1 after they're attacked."f\bAlso, they won't be effective in Titan Challenge; all opponents there are immune to stat drops."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."S\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now.  Get ready and take care now!"M\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now.  Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."^\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold.  An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."s\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision.  This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"Y\bHey, partner! Can I interest you in some moves? They don't have these anywhere else, you know.\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas,Dual Wingbeat, Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam,Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage, Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]" \bCome again! Or not. Hehe."\bAny other moves?\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas, Dual Wingbeat,Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam, Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage,Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now.  Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here?  You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations!  So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"t\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players.  Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"[\bAlright, you got so far!  What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players.  I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"V\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand.  Sheesh. :)"_\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it.  Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."U\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE.  Would you like to enter?"|\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Galar,Hisui,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rAwwww, be careful out there. *wink*"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs</i>. <i>Sobs</i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bIn this challenge specifically, you also won't be able to inflict your opponents with status conditions, flinch, trap or confuse them!"�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"{\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Titan Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your mons alive!"i\bAlso, they won't be effective here in the Titan Challenge; all opponents are immune to stat drops."!\bFoul: Why hello there pal!"\bAre you lost?"�\bTook the wrong turn looking for the bathroom? Well don't you worry, just follow me and I will take you back to where you're supposed to be."9\bOh who am I kidding. We both know you're not lost."f\bThis is one of the most secure facilities in this dimension; people don't just get "lost" here."t\bYour luck seems to have run out now that I've found you before the other two, see, I'm not as nice as them..."!\bBut then again, I'm bored."\bEhhh, why not."~\bSee, it would be mean if I defeated you now, but wouldn't it be even meaner if I healed you, just to make you wipe out?"+\bLet me show you what I mean by that!"<\bNot too bad, maybe you do have some skills after all."L\bNow scram and make sure I don't catch you sneaking around here again!"d\bBut maybe leave a resume on your way out. We might need someone of your talent in the future."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."L\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there.  MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round..."0\r*sighs* I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."w\rVermint: Hello \PN, I hope you enjoy your stay here.  Try not to think too much about our first encounter, okay?"W\rVermint: Hello \PN, I had foreseen that I would have to introduce myself to you."^\rMy true name is Vera. I created your wardrobe and I am also here to judge your resolve."-\rI hope this isn't a shock to you, \PN."bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."JYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"FAn ominous Vending Machine stares at you. Best not to go near it."=PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS ENEMY SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"vYou can't seem to get the Vending Machine to work anymore. Maybe it can only be used before starting a challenge?"#The exit seems to be locked..."?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"c\bLuc-ker: Oh, you want to battle me at my full power? Fine, but don't say you weren't warned."G\bLuc: Too easy, huh? I lied - that wasn't actually my full power."�\bMy real master, Yhwach, gifted me with the shift V - The Visionary, turning my imagination into reality! That means I can throw at you whatever I can conjure and I simply haven't had enough to imagine yet."\bUntil next time!"Z\bLuc: Hehe, that's a taste of what's to come soon. Thanks for letting me go all-out!"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then."C\rDid you know that there's a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."�\rHow do you know if you're strong? I heard another rumour that, if you get good in Club, and I mean <i>real good</i> in Club, they'll acknowledge you."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"_\rHuh? You don't know what I'm talking about?  Hahaha, you haven't lost to them, have you?"X\rYou're either really good, or you haven't been whooped yet. Either way, have fun!"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."1\ch[98,-1,Display your Staff Pass,Walk Away]"b\bOh, you are one of the staff here? You should have show me your pass earlier. Please enter."\bPlease leave. Thank you."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE.  Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your original bag back soon enough.">\bYou have a Backstage Pass. Let me tear that up for you."R\bHow strange. You don't seem to have a backstage pass. Try buying one again." \bPlease let me escort you."�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"T\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you, \PN! (The hyphen is important by the way.)"�\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics. By the way, you can call me Luc for short if my full name is too hard for you."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"~\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Finish]"W\bThe Club Challenge - here, you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"x\bYou'll be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle.  If you do well enough, you might get some... *ahem* privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no items, so it's a good place to grind your Pokémon!"}\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, the challenge that chucks trainers at you until your team drops (or until you defeat 150 trainers)."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."�\bYour longest, most glorious run will be logged for you so you can boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"x\bThe Mayhem Challenge - in this one, you battle with trainers in a full battles and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's because they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You'll never know what's up their sleeves!"^\bThey have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge; you'll battle "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge you'll be battling Sync Pokémon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."}YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT.  PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION.\ch[98,-1,View active buffs,Other options?,Close menu]"iThe other options have been grayed out. Maybe they can only be accessed before starting a challenge?"\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b40 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!"2\b\v[61] GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same.".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?"9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day."e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."^\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE.  Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?"*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL OFFER DEAL***, Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits), Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems (1 Credit), Held Items,Credit-Money Exchange]"o\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits), VIP Backstage Pass (5 Credits), Grandeur Club Staff Pass (500 Credits)]"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME.""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"0BACKSTAGE PASS NOT FOR SALE YET! THANK YOU!".BACKSTAGE PASS ALREADY BOUGHT! THANK YOU!"7YOU ALREADY OWN A STAFF PASS. COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"XLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD!  THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Master"Challenge"Win Counts"Cancel"Backstage"	Yes?"No!;[�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!".\rWould you like to recieve some healing?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"o\rCan't believe you made me fully restore your team, you bastard. This wasn't supposed to even be a thing."`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."9\rYour team should already be at full health, right?"8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto, Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary, Neo Champion,Sygna Buffs]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto, Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary,Neo Champion]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."�\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying! That is, if you don't hit F12 because you're a sore loser or a tryhard."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bThey'll also have some interesting moves too, ranging from moves used by their trainers instead or powerful moves that can only be used under certain conditions."�\bFuthermore, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"�\bBut lastly, and you might find a silver lining in this - I've made it so that not only do you benefit from some damage reduction, the "harder" trainers have a lower chance to show up early."�\bSo if you want to familiarise yourself with the trainers here, it might be good to try this challenge with a lower difficulty first.".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure. Which one would you like me to explain? \ch[1,-1,Crit Rate,Trainer Move,B Move,Passive Skill, Master Passive,Zone,Gradual Healing]"R\bCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages."�\bTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses (rather than their Pokémon). These moves tend to buff the user's Pokémon or their team's side."^\bThey can be used even when the trainer's Pokémon is afflicted with a status condition."}\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. You can identify them by the "descriptor" in the move's name, e.g. Origin Volt Tackle."~\bThey tend to do what the move they're based on does, but with increased power, added effects or the regular effect enhanced."\bThere's usually a condition that has to be met before each B Move can be used, so use that to your advantage to counter them!"�\bIf they don't, they will likely have very little PP instead. Lastly, all trainers only have 1 B Move at most, but there is 1 exception."mPassive Skill - Essentially an extra ability, but they can't be ignored by effects such as Mold Breaker."~\bHow many a Pokémon has is completely arbitrary, though I've tried to limit it to 3 at most, excluding Master Passives."l\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the team's damage dealt and reduces the damage taken."k\bThere are 3 types: Flag Bearer is for all moves and is 10% damage increase and 20% damage reduction."W\bPride is for physical moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."_\bLastly, Spirit is for special moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."`\bZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type by 50%."s\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn. Think of it kinda like Leftovers."T\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika, Red,Red (Thunderbolt),Blue,Leaf]"W\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit."�\bAnyway, his Trainer Move give his Tyranitar's +1 Defense and makes its next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but there are ways to get around it, like Protect."�\bTtar has 2 passives. One gives its moves a higher chance to apply their additional effects and the other prevents its stats from dropping in a sandstorm."s\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move gives her Vaporeon +2 Defense and her side +2 Sp. Defense."�\bLastly, her Vaporeon's passives give it gradual healing when switching in as well as a chance to raise its Evasion after it uses a move."}\bErika's Trainer Move gives her Leafeon's +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, but if the Sun's up, these stat increases are doubled."`\bLeafeon's ability is Chorophyll, so with the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled."t\bThen, its passives don't allow status conditions to be inflicted on it as well as heal it after using a move."@\bIn other words, you really don't want Leafeon in the Sun!"�\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Charizard's +3 Attack, Sp. Attack and Speed and +2 Crit Rate, though its Defense and Sp. Defense are lowered by -1."{\bHis Charizard also has passives which allow its moves to never miss and not require a rechage turn after using them."X\bKnow what that means? It's able to use Blast Burn. Every. Single. Turn. Have fun!"s\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move gives Pikachu +6 Attack and Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since there you only use 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair per battle."h\bIt also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."{\bIts other passives make all its moves critical hits, as well as healing it after it uses a move in Electric Terrain."q\bLast, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a B Move which can only be used when Electric Terrain's active."X\bIf your Pokémon's paralyzed, its Defense and Sp. Defense are also lowered by -1."r\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Defense and +1 Crit Rate, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."~\bAnyway, his Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, one of its passive gives his side +1 Attack and Sp. Attack."�\bAnd then when it attacks, its other passive gives its side +1 Sp. Defense. Lastly, it also doesn't need to recharge after using Hydro Cannon."`\bWith Leaf's Trainer Move, I took a few creative liberties to make it live up to its name."q\bIt provides the Pokémon on her side Gradual Healing, as well as healing them all for 40% of their max HP!"�\bAs for Venusaur's passives, they badly poison your Pokémon and gives them -1 to their defensive stats after they're attacked by it."h\bWith Razor Leaf and a non-recharging Frenzy Plant, it's sure to deal out a ton poison and damage."Y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris, Silver,Giovanni,Giovanni (Ultra)]"q\bMorty's Trainer Move gives +1 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate to his side, as well as setting Tailwind."�\bOne of Ho-oh's passives gives additional stat boosts to its team if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."a\bIts other passive then heals the Pokémon on Ho- oh's side when it uses a move in the Sun."s\bEthan's Trainer Move powers up Lugia's next special move, gives it +1 Accuracy and makes its next move crit."{\bLugia has passives which makes its single target attacks hit all opponents as well as restore PP to Ethan's Trainer Move."k\bLastly, it also has a Spirit Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bLyra's Trainer Move gives +2 Attack and Sp. Attack to a Pokémon on her side and gives them Gradual Healing. But that's not the crazy thing about this sync pair."�\bCelebi has passives which leaves the opponent flinched, trapped and confused after using a move and lowers one of the target's stats by -2."v\bAnnnnd Celebi has Grassy Glide and can set up Grassy Terrain too to give it priority. Talk about a nasty combo!"j\bLastly, it also has a Pride Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."N\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers."O\bAt base, her Trainer Move gives her side +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate."{\bBut if it's Raining, it also powers up the next special attack from her team, making them pack an even bigger punch."�\bOne of Suicune's passives gives its side +4 Sp. Defense if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."�\bIts other passive heals its team after a uses a move under the Rain. I think you get the idea - Rain is dangerous if you're facing Kris!"k\bLastly, it has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."k\bSilver's Trainer Move gives Sneasel +3 Attack and Speed, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."�\bSneasel's B Move, Crushing Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. In theory, that doesn't sound too hard to counter, right?"\bWell, on every hit of a multi-hit move, its passives lower the opposing Pokémon's Speed by -1 while it gets +1 Evasion."~\bIt also gets +1 Crit Rate on each hit of its B Move too, but it doesn't have any other ways of increasing its damage itself."N\bSo at best, you get lucky and OHKO it, while at worst, it's a nuisance."<\bGiovanni's Trainer Move gives his Nidoking +6 Attack."a\bHis Nidoking has a passive to make all its attacks critical hits, including its Max Moves."�\bIts other passive turns Normal moves into Ground moves, allowing it to gain STAB from it. Its Mega Kick is going to hit pretty hard!"�\bThis version of Giovanni has a Trainer Move which gives his side +2 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as making Guzzlord the center of attention."{\bGuzzlord has passives which enable its Stockpile Defense and Sp. Defense boosts to be tripled and shared with its allies."O\bHowever, it can only Stockpile a maximum of 2 times as a result of this."�\bGuzzlord also doesn't have just 1 B Move, but 2! It's the one exception to the "rule" that says there can only be 1 B Move for each sync pair."i\bWhen used, they both remove Stockpiles's stat boosts and restores 1 PP to Giovanni's Trainer Move."�\bThe first one, Guzzling Swallow, can only be used after Stockpile has been used and restores Guzzlord's HP based on how many times it was used."=\bThen, it restores a fixed amount of HP for its allies."�\bThe second one is Gourging Crunch. It can only be used when the Guzzlord's stat boosts for Defense and Sp. Defense are 6 or greater."9\bIt then lowers the target's defensive stats by -1.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Blaziken +4 Attack and +1 Accuracy, sets up Tailwind and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."�\bBlaziken's first passive gives +1 Speed to its side when entering battle, including Mega Evolution, effectively translating to a +2 increase."�\bIts other passive lowers the target's Defense by -2. All in all, very speedy and it can easily snowball if you're not careful."c\bBrendan's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense as well as +1 Crit Rate."u\bHis Latios's first passive powers up its sides' next special moves when entering the battle and Mega Evolving."x\bIts other passive then increases the likelihood of additional effects; if it's a stat drop, it'll be doubled too."p\bIt has Luster Purge, so that'll mean that you'll be taking a lot of special damage if you're not careful!"�\bSteven... is a lot. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4! So let's break him down a bit.\ch[2,-1,Initial State,Shared Traits, Normal Forme,Attack Forme,Defense Forme,Speed Forme]"\bInitially, Deoxys starts in its Normal Forme with 4 Trainer Moves and a passive which gives it +1 Accuracy when switching in."�\bThe first one, "Try This!", sets Psychic Terrain and gives Deoxys +2 Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed and keep Deoxys in its Normal Forme."u\bHis second one, "Attack!", gives Deoxys +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme."�\bThe third one, "Defend!" gives its +4 side Attack and Sp. Attack. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn."r\bLast but not least,"Faster!", gives Deoxys +6 Speed and +3 Evasion and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme."�\bOutside of its inital state, all forms of Deoxys that Steven has have a passive with converts stat drops into stat increases, but not vice versa like Contrary does!"a\bThey all also have Psycho Boost and Zen Headbutt, so I won't be mentioning them elsewhere."`\bIn its Normal Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."{\bIt also has a passive which increase the chance of additional effects, so if it uses Zen Headbutt, be prepared to flinch!"`\bIn its Attack Forme, Deoxys has Protect and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which increases the power of its next physical and special moves, so it might quickly snowball out of control!"a\bIn its Defense Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Iron Defense in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which gives its side +2 Sp. Defense each time a status move is used, so with Iron Defense it'll become very bulky very quickly."^\bIn its Speed Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Double Team in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which sets up Tailwind for its side when a status move is successful the first time it's used in battle."_\bWally's Trainer Move gives his Gardevoir +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Sp. Defense and Crit Rate."�\bGardevoir has 2 passives - the first gives its side +1 Speed when entering battle and Mega Evolving; the other leaves the target confused after a move."�\bGardevoir also has a B Move, Ultimate Dazzling Gleam. It lowers the targets' Attack and Sp. Attack by -4, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks."�\bIt can only be used once, but you can't Protect against it and -4 on your attacking stats will likely force you to switch out your Pokémon."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."�\bApart from that, Kommo-o has passives which allow it to ignore damage reduction from Reflect, Light Screen and Aurora Veil as well as increase the chance for additional effects."�\bThis version of Cynthia's Trainer Move gives Giratina +4 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate. She can also set a Ghost Zone."T\bHer Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Sp. Defense of the target by -1."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move gives her side +4 Defense and Sp. Defense, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll give +6 instead."r\bAs for that, her Lucario has a passive which sets Fighting Zone on entry, so most of the time, it'll be +6."s\bLucario's other passive also depends on Fighting Zone - it heals its side after using a move if it's active."y\bIt also has Superior Aura Sphere, a B Move that never misses and can only be used after Lucario is attacked twice."]\bAfter it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of its side."p\bLastly, Lucario has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."\bCyrus's Trainer Move gives his Darkrai +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy and Crit Rate. In addition, he can set a Dark Zone."�\bDarkrai has passives which power up its moves if the target is asleep, or if it's using a status move, it'll lower a random stat of all opponents by -1."[\bIt does have Dark Void, but even if it misses, its 2nd passive will activate anyway."�\bDawn's Trainer Move gives her side +2 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP."^\bYou might be thinking, why do that, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"i\bCresselia's very tanky, but one of its passives makes it even more so when it has 50% HP or lower."�\bIts other passive also increases the power of its side's special moves if Cresselia uses a status move when it's HP is 50% or lower."P\bIt also has Moonlight for healing, so don't count your chickens too soon!"R\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N, Roxie,Ingo,Emmet]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move gives +2 Accuracy and Crit Rate to a Pokémon on her side, as well as giving +2 Sp. Attack to all Pokémon on her side."�\bRotom has a passive which gives it +1 Evasion when it's hit, as well as another which prevents its Evasion from being lowered."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it gives +6 Attack and Evasion and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition, it has passives which increase the chance of the additional effects its moves and increase their power when Sharpedo is in a pinch."s\bHilbert's Trainer Move gives his Genesect +3 Sp. Attack, +2 Crit Rate and powers up its next special attack."�\bWhen using Techno Blast, Genesect changes form depending on the type the target is weakest to. Its default is also Bug instead of Normal."]\bThen, it makes them weaker to that type and applies an effect corresponding that type."m\bElectric - Paralyze target.\n Fire - Lower target's Attack by -1.\n Ice - 50% chance to freeze target."H\bWater - Lower target's Defense by -1. Bug - No additional effect."d\bLastly, if Genesect lands a super effective hit, its passive lowers the target's Speed by -2."�\bHilda's Trainer Move raises her Victini's Sp. Attack by how much its Attack has been raised, then gives it +3 Crit Rate and gives its team +1 Accuracy."�\bThis is complemented by Victini's passives, which gives it +2 Attack on switching in and turns stat drops into stat increases."y\bThere's even more synergy - Victini has V-Create, so it just keeps getting bulkier and faster each time it's used!"D\bN's Trainer Move gives his Kyurem +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bWhen Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it has a passive which halves the damage it takes while charging and unlocks its B Move, Resonating Noble Roar."|\bIt lowers the Attack, Sp. Attack, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by -2, while it powering up its next physical attack."�\bFreeze Shock then needs to be used again before it can be used again, preventing it from being spammed endlessly (it also has 3 PP)."�\bKyurem also has a passive which allows it to ignore the opponent's enduring effects, but I imagine that won't come up too often."q\bRoxie's Trainer Move gives her Toxtricity +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate and applies Tailwind to her side."W\bToxtricity has has 2 passives. One sets Poison Zone on switch in and extends it."e\bThe other lowers the target's Attack or Sp. Attack if it's poisoned or paralyzed respectively."~\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Frenzied Sludge Wave. It can only be used if there's an opponent with a status condition."�\bIt can't be protected against, lowers the target's Sp. Defense by -2 and poisons it if it doesn't already have a status condition."^\bIngo's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. His Chandelure can Dynamax."�\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as increasing the power of its team's next special moves."�\bIt also has a B Move, Rising Flames Hex. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."�\bIt applies effects based on what the target's inflicted with:\nParalysis - Lower target's Defense by -2.\n Burn - Lower target's Sp. Defense by -2."^\bPoison - Heal itself and allies for a little HP.\n Flinch - Lower target's Speed by -2."b\bTrap - Power up user's next physical move.\n Confusion - Power up user's next special move."�\bEmmet's Trainer Move gives a Pokémon on his side Ground immunity for 5 turns and makes its next moves critical hits. His Eelektross can Dynamax."m\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as trapping the target."�\bIt also has a B Move, Descending Lightning Wild Charge. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"g\bSerena's Trainer Move gives her +6 Zygarde's Attack and Sp. Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."\\bZygarde's passives prevent its stats from being lowered and its attacks from missing."p\bLastly, it also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move gives her Marshadow +4 Attack and +3 Speed and Evasion. After attacking, Marshadow's passive raises one of its stats by +1 3 times."|\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Sp. Defense by the same amount of stages."`\bThen, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."x\bDiancie's B Move, Pink Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up."M\bIt lowers the target's Defense by -2 while giving its side +2 Defense."�\bDiancie's passives lower all opponents' Speed by -1 when entering battle and Mega Evolving, as well as giving it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate after using a move."_\bLysandre's Trainer Move gives his +4 Volcanion Sp. Attack, +1 Accuracy and +3 Crit Rate."�\bVolcanion itself has one passive which burns the targets that it hits. This is then complimented with its B Move, Heat Hydro Pump."�\bIt can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned and is an AoE move which deals more damage to burned targets."o\bThen, based on how many burned targets it hits, it makes Volcanion's next special attack do more damage."I\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana, Acerola,Mina,Gladion]"v\bLusamine's Trainer Move gives Necrozma +6 Sp. Attack and -1 Speed. Her Dusk-Mane Necrozma can also Ultra Burst."�\bIt also has passives which turns its single target moves into AoE moves and allows Prismatic Laser to be used without the user recharging."M\bHau's Trainer Move gives his Tapu Koko +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."z\bWhen entering battle, one of Koko's passives extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next special attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."l\bThen, Koko's B Move, Wild Electroweb, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the Speed of all targets by -2 while +2 Speed to Koko and its allies."H\bLana's Trainer Move gives her Tapu Lele +6 Attack and Sp. Attack."y\bWhen entering battle, one of Lele's passives extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up its next physical and special attacks when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."{\bLastly, its B Move, Neo Psycho Cut, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move gives +2 Defense and +3 Crit Rate to her side's Pokémon. If it's Sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), it gives +2 Attack too."v\bWhen entering battle, Bulu's first passive extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next physical attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."t\bLastly, its B Move, Unbreakable Swords Dance, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."b\bIt gives +2 Attack to Bulu and its allies makes their next physical attacks do more damage."�\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side and gives +4 Sp. Attack (+6 if Raining) and Gradual Healing to the Pokémon on her side."x\bWhen entering battle, Tapu Fini's ability sets Fairy Zone (because Misty Terrain sucks) and extends its duration."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which gives its side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."p\bLastly, Fini's B Move, Sea Deity Protect, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt applies Protect to itself and its allies, then it restores 20% HP (30% with Fairy Zone) for itself and its allies and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's Raining."q\bGladion's Trainer Move gives his Magearna +6 Sp. Attack, +3 Crit Rate and powers up its next special move."�\bMagearna has passives which lower the target's Sp. Attack by -2 after using a move and prevent its own stats from being lowered."]\bThen, Magearna's B Move, Piercing Fleur Cannon, can only be used after it uses a move."}\bIts power and the power of its next special move increases based on how much the targets' Sp. Attack has been lowered.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon,Piers,Gloria (Dojo)]"o\bLeon's Trainer Move gives his Eternatus +3 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate but lowers its Sp. Defense by -1."�\bHis Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and one of its passives enables its Eternabeam to not require a recharge turn after it's used."~\bIts other passive also lowers the target's Attack, Defense, Sp. Attack, Sp. Defense, Speed, Accuracy and Evasion by -1."O\bPier's Trainer Move gives his Toxtricity +2 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."�\bToxtricity has passives which set Electric Terrain and extend it on switch in, as well as ignore the target's enduring effects."}\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Sorrowful Echos Overdrive. It can only be used if there's an active weather, terrain or zone."�\bIt also can't be protected against and does more damage if the target has a status condition, which would most likely happen from its Sludge Bomb."Z\bGloria's Trainer Move gives her Urshifu +3 Attack. Her Urshifu can also Gigantamax."p\bOther than that, it just has passives which lower the target's Defense and Speed by -1 when hitting them."j\bWith Surging Strikes, it'll apply to each hit, so you'll actually end up with -3 Defense and Speed!"v\bNice choice! These guys were made for PoMas's anniversaries and are much simpler compared to the Neo Champions."m\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lillie (2022),N (2022),Steven (2022), May (2023),Skyla (2023),Raihan (2023)]"l\bFun fact: This is my favourite anniversary trainer out of them all! Her skirt is sooo good... anyway!"m\bLillie's Trainer Move gives her Lunala +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, the first of its kind in PoMas."b\bIts passives set Tailwind when its switched in and powers up its moves when its HP is full."r\bN's Trainer Move gives his Reshiram +3 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy, as well as setting Tailwind on his side."v\bIts passives turn its single target moves into AoE moves and lower the target's Sp. Defense after attacking it."K\bSteven's Trainer Move gives his Rayquaza +2 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."a\bIts passives turn stat drops into stat increases and gives it +1 Speed after using a move."{\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Latias +2 Defense and Sp. Defense and +3 Crit Rate, as well as setting Tailwind on her side."s\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and doubles stat drops that it inflicts."s\bSkyla's Trainer Move gives her Tornadus +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as giving her side +2 Speed."v\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and confuses the target after attacking it."�\bRaihan's Trainer Move gives his Flygon +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate, then powers up his team's next physical and special moves."�\bIts passives power up its team's next physical and special moves when using a status move and when attacking a target that's flinching, trapped or confused, it lowers its attacking stats by -1."&\bLastly, his Flygon can Dynamax."n\bHoho! All of these guys have a Master Passive (I'm assuming you know what that is by now) and a B Move."y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Calem,Marnie, Hop,Bede,Red,Leaf,Blue,Nate,Rosa,Silver,Cheren, Bianca,May,Brendan]"w\bSerena has quite a lot going on, so let's split her kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"n\bSerena is quite interesting. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."\bThe simplest part of her kit is definitely her Trainer Move. It gives her Greninja +2 Attack, +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."5\bHer Greninja also has a Spirit Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which max out the number of hits of a multi-strike move and for each hit, it lowers a random stat of the target by -1."T\bThat means its Water Shuriken will always end up lowering your stats 5 times!"z\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which lower the target's Accuracy by -1 and has a chance of making it flinch."b\bBoundless Quick Attack won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"�\bIt makes the target weaker to Greninja's current type, as well as lower its Defense and Sp. Defense by -2 and give its side +3 Speed."v\bCalem has quite a lot going on, so let's split his kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"g\bCalem is pretty cool. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."�\bThe simplest part of his kit is definitely his Trainer Move. It gives his side +4 Attack, +2 Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, then sets up Tailwind."4\bHis Greninja also has a Pride Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to status conditions, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in the rain."�\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to stat drops, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in a Dark Zone."h\bTransformational Double Team won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"c\bWhen Greninja's a Water type, it'll make it rain and power up its side's next special moves."i\bIf it's a Dark type, it'll set up a Dark Zone and power up its side's next physical moves instead."S\bThen regardless of type, it'll also give Greninja and its allies +2 Evasion."�\bMarnie's Trainer Move gives her Galarian Moltres +6 Sp. Attack, +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. It then takes 10% of its max HP as recoil damage."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives give it +3 Crit Rate when switching in and powers up its moves when it's not at max HP."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fierce Fiery Wrath, can only be used after 2 other moves have been used. It can't be protected against and flinchest its target(s)."q\bHop's Trainer Move gives his Galarian Zapdos +3 Speed and -1 Sp. Defense. It then sets up a Fighting Zone."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives give it +2 Attack on entry and lower the target's Sp. Defense when lowering its Defense."�\bLastly, its B Move, Roaring Thunderous Kick, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It lowers the target's Defense by -3."�\bBede's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Attack, Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, as well as powering up his side's next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives give its side +1 Speed on entry and makes it immune to critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Intimidating Freezing Glare, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It gives his side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."i\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Kantonian Articuno +6 Sp. Attack and powers up its next special move."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, it has quite a few other passives. First off, its moves will always land and be critical hits."�\bThen, it lowers its target's resistance to ice moves and powers up its next special attack based on how many opponents its move hit."�\bLastly, its B Move, Frozen Wings Ice Beam, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type and freezes the target."a\bLeaf's Trainer Move gives her Kantonian Moltres +6 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."Z\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its passives supercharge its status moves."�\bIn addition to their original effects, it makes them lower the target's Attack, Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense by -1 and makes it weaker to Fire moves."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fiery Wings Flare Blitz, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type. It burns the target and double its stat drops."z\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as powering up their next special moves."^\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its passives make its moves very potent."�\bIn addition to their original effects, they make the target weaker to Electric moves and give Zapdos's side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."r\bLastly, its B Move, Thundering Wings Roost, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type."�\bIt heals Zapdos and its allies for 60% and 30% of their respective max HPs, gives its side Gradual Healing and removes all their status conditions."d\bNate's Trainer Move returns his Haxorus's lowered stats back to normal and gives it +3 Speed."~\bWith Nate using his Trainer Move, one of Haxorus's passives will also give it +6 Attack and power up its next physical move."`\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passive makes its moves critical hits."f\bLastly, its B Move, Dark Black Outrage, can only be used when Haxorus's Attack has been raised."�\bRosa's Trainer Move gives her side a boost to her team's special or physical moves when Meloetta is in its Aria or Pirouette forms respectively."}\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives play around the fact that Meloetta has 2 different forms."U\bFirst off, its Normal moves become the same type as Meloetta's secondary type."�\bAfter using a move, it then give its side +1 Defense or Sp. Defense (Pirouette and Aria respectively) and makes its target weaker to Meloetta's second type."p\bLastly, its B Move, Relic Song of Wonder, can only be used when Meloetta is at 1/3 or more of its max HP."�\bIt changes Meloetta's form and powers up its side's next physical and special moves and has a chance to make the target fall asleep."{\bSilver's Trainer Move gives his Tyranitar +6 Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as +1 Accuracy if used in a Sandstorm."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives strengthen it in a Sandstorm. First, it extends the duration of Sandstorms."\bIts moves also get powered up in a Sandstorm and it also gets a boost to its next physical attack after using an attack."�\bLastly, its B Move, Massive Rock Slide, always flinches its target(s) but can't be used consecutively or on Ttar's first turn in battle."�\bCheren's Trainer Move gives his Tornadus +4 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as powering it its next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives make its moves always land, be critical hits, then strengthen its next physical and special moves."y\bLastly, its B Move, Black Gale Bleakwind Storm, can't be used consecutively or on Tornadus's first turn in battle."}\bIt increases in power based on how much its next physical move would be powered up and lower the target's Speed by -2."}\bIn addition, if it's used as Tornadus's 2nd move after entering battle, it makes the target(s) weaker to Flying moves."K\bBianca's Trainer Move gives her Virizion +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives allow gives its side +1 Speed and Evasion after using a move and ignore enduring."�\bLastly, its B Move, White Light Sacred Sword, lowers the target's attacking stats by -3 and makes its weaker to Fighting moves."A\bIt also ignores the target's defensive and evasive boosts."�\bMay's Trainer Move powers up the next special move of a Pokémon on her side and her Kyogre, as well as giving the latter +2 Sp. Attack."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Sp. Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Blue Origin Pulse, can only be used in Heavy Rain. It lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Sp. Defense by -3."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move powers up the next physical move of a Pokémon on his side and his Groudon, as well as giving the latter +2 Attack."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."v\bLastly, its B Move, Red Precipice Blades, lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Defense by -2."v\bHowever, it can only be used in Harsh Sun and can't be used consecutively or on Groudon's first turn in battle."z\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bEssentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are 5 types of buffs: Blessings, Immunities, Restoration, Boosters and Crushers."q\bWhat buff type would you like to know about? \ch[1,-1,Blessings,Immunities,Restoration,Boosters, Crushers]"\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat increases at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level."�\bIn addition, you can buy an enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assasin's Blessing) for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bAs an example, Warrior's Blessing Lv. 1 will give your Pokémon +1 Attack when they enter battle, essentially giving them Intrepid Sword!"�\bImmunites make your Pokémon immune to status conditions, "interferences" (i.e. flinching, trapping and confusion) or even critical hits for some time."Q\bAll of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."�\bHowever, once you buy out the whole store, you can then buy buffs that make you immune to all status conditions and interferences."<\bThey will use up 4 and 3 energy respectively, though."�\bIf you talk to Nurse Joy now, she'll actually heal your team now! But... just a little bit, if you don't give her any energy. Better than nothing though, amirite?"�\bAt base, she'll heal your team for 10% of its HP, as well as restore 1/8 of its PP (restoring at least 1 PP per move, though)."�\bThe restoration buffs increase those amounts though. For each level of the HP Recovery buff, she'll heal 25%, 50% and 100% of your team's HP."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your 'mons alive!"m\bFor each level of the PP Recovery buff, it'll restore 1/4, 1/2 and all of your team's PP respectively."�\bFurthermore, she also won't remove status conditions from your team; you'll have to equip the Status Recovery buff first! It costs 3 energy."�\bLastly, these buffs are only active in the Sync Challenge. If she gave any healing in the Titan Challenge, it would be wayyy too easy!"}\bBoosters give your Pokémon +1 to a stat (except Accuracy and Evasion) after they use a move, even if the move failed."Q\bAll of them use 1 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."l\bCrushers lowers one of the target's stats (except Accuracy and Evasion) by -1 after they're attacked."f\bAlso, they won't be effective in Titan Challenge; all opponents there are immune to stat drops."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."R\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Get ready and take care now!"L\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."]\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold. An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."r\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision. This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"Y\bHey, partner! Can I interest you in some moves? They don't have these anywhere else, you know.\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas,Dual Wingbeat, Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam,Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage, Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]" \bCome again! Or not. Hehe."\bAny other moves?\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas, Dual Wingbeat,Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam, Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage,Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now. Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here? You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations! So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"s\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players. Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"Z\bAlright, you got so far! What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players. I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"U\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand. Sheesh. :)"^\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it. Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."T\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"|\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Galar,Hisui,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rAwwww, be careful out there. *wink*"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs</i>. <i>Sobs</i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bIn this challenge specifically, you also won't be able to inflict your opponents with status conditions, flinch, trap or confuse them!"�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"{\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Titan Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your mons alive!"i\bAlso, they won't be effective here in the Titan Challenge; all opponents are immune to stat drops."!\bFoul: Why hello there pal!"\bAre you lost?"�\bTook the wrong turn looking for the bathroom? Well don't you worry, just follow me and I will take you back to where you're supposed to be."9\bOh who am I kidding. We both know you're not lost."f\bThis is one of the most secure facilities in this dimension; people don't just get "lost" here."t\bYour luck seems to have run out now that I've found you before the other two, see, I'm not as nice as them..."!\bBut then again, I'm bored."\bEhhh, why not."~\bSee, it would be mean if I defeated you now, but wouldn't it be even meaner if I healed you, just to make you wipe out?"+\bLet me show you what I mean by that!"<\bNot too bad, maybe you do have some skills after all."L\bNow scram and make sure I don't catch you sneaking around here again!"d\bBut maybe leave a resume on your way out. We might need someone of your talent in the future."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."K\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round..."0\r*sighs* I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."v\rVermint: Hello \PN, I hope you enjoy your stay here. Try not to think too much about our first encounter, okay?"W\rVermint: Hello \PN, I had foreseen that I would have to introduce myself to you."^\rMy true name is Vera. I created your wardrobe and I am also here to judge your resolve."-\rI hope this isn't a shock to you, \PN."bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."JYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"FAn ominous Vending Machine stares at you. Best not to go near it."=PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS ENEMY SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"vYou can't seem to get the Vending Machine to work anymore. Maybe it can only be used before starting a challenge?"#The exit seems to be locked..."?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"c\bLuc-ker: Oh, you want to battle me at my full power? Fine, but don't say you weren't warned."G\bLuc: Too easy, huh? I lied - that wasn't actually my full power."�\bMy real master, Yhwach, gifted me with the shift V - The Visionary, turning my imagination into reality! That means I can throw at you whatever I can conjure and I simply haven't had enough to imagine yet."\bUntil next time!"Z\bLuc: Hehe, that's a taste of what's to come soon. Thanks for letting me go all-out!"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then."C\rDid you know that there's a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."�\rHow do you know if you're strong? I heard another rumour that, if you get good in Club, and I mean <i>real good</i> in Club, they'll acknowledge you."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"^\rHuh? You don't know what I'm talking about? Hahaha, you haven't lost to them, have you?"X\rYou're either really good, or you haven't been whooped yet. Either way, have fun!"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."1\ch[98,-1,Display your Staff Pass,Walk Away]"b\bOh, you are one of the staff here? You should have show me your pass earlier. Please enter."\bPlease leave. Thank you."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"P\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your original bag back soon enough.">\bYou have a Backstage Pass. Let me tear that up for you."R\bHow strange. You don't seem to have a backstage pass. Try buying one again." \bPlease let me escort you."�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"T\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you, \PN! (The hyphen is important by the way.)"�\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics. By the way, you can call me Luc for short if my full name is too hard for you."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"~\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Finish]"W\bThe Club Challenge - here, you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"w\bYou'll be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle. If you do well enough, you might get some... *ahem* privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no items, so it's a good place to grind your Pokémon!"}\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, the challenge that chucks trainers at you until your team drops (or until you defeat 150 trainers)."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."�\bYour longest, most glorious run will be logged for you so you can boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"x\bThe Mayhem Challenge - in this one, you battle with trainers in a full battles and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's because they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You'll never know what's up their sleeves!"^\bThey have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge; you'll battle "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge you'll be battling Sync Pokémon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."|YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION.\ch[98,-1,View active buffs,Other options?,Close menu]"iThe other options have been grayed out. Maybe they can only be accessed before starting a challenge?"\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b40 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!"2\b\v[61] GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same.".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?"9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day."e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."]\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE. Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?"*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL OFFER DEAL***, Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits), Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems (1 Credit), Held Items,Credit-Money Exchange]"o\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits), VIP Backstage Pass (5 Credits), Grandeur Club Staff Pass (500 Credits)]"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME.""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"0BACKSTAGE PASS NOT FOR SALE YET! THANK YOU!".BACKSTAGE PASS ALREADY BOUGHT! THANK YOU!"7YOU ALREADY OWN A STAFF PASS. COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"WLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Master"Challenge"Win Counts"Cancel"Backstage"	Yes?"No!Iu;␀�	[[%"-Celadon City Pokémon Gym Leader:\nErika" The Nature-Loving Princess!")\bThis is my trusted pal, Poliwrath."=\bIt evolved from a Poliwhirl when I used a Water Stone."2\bThis might help you beat the P1 Grand Prix."&\bUse it well and win that thing."!\bGary: How's it going, \PN?"J\bWhat? You only have four badges? What a loser! I already have five.")\bAnd how many Pokémon do you have?"_\bThat's not nearly as many as me! You'll never catch up to the legendary Gary Oak. Later!"C\rI got my Koffing in Cinnabar. It breathes poison when angry."&My boyfriend taught me this move."Want to learn Covet?"Come back anytime!"\rPoli"3Find what you need at the Celadon Dept. Store!"(Would you like to take it with you?"'There's no more room for Pokémon!";The Pokémon Boxes are full and can't accept any more!"+\bMoan...\nI blew it all in the slots!":\bI knew I should have cashed in my Coins for prizes!"\bKoff Koffing".\bThis Gym is great!\nIt's full of women!"/Game Corner\nThe playground for grown-ups!"(The Pokémon Number One Grand Prix!"\rChansey"-Celadon City\nThe City of Rainbow Dreams"0Coins exchanged for prizes!\nPrize Exchange"E\rCeladon takes pride in its efforts to keep the city beautiful.">\rThat's why the Game Corner is bad for our city's image."Yes"No[%"-Celadon City Pokémon Gym Leader:\nErika" The Nature-Loving Princess!")\bThis is my trusted pal, Poliwrath."=\bIt evolved from a Poliwhirl when I used a Water Stone."2\bThis might help you beat the P1 Grand Prix."&\bUse it well and win that thing."!\bGary: How's it going, \PN?"K\bWhat? You only have four badges?  What a loser! I already have five.")\bAnd how many Pokémon do you 